    <node id="task_29">
      <data key="d0">desc_generated</data>
      <data key="d1">generated</data>
      <data key="d2">Objective: Descend from the overworld into the dungeon after defeating a zombie, teaching the descend action and the kill‑to‑clear level mechanic.

Description: The agent must find the ladder down, kill a zombie that guards it (because the ladder is locked until one hostile mob is killed), and use the DESCEND action to enter the dungeon. Survival pressure is dramatically reduced so the agent can concentrate on combat and descent. A wood sword is provided from the start, eliminating any need to craft. A single zombie is pre‑placed near the ladder. All other mob spawns are disabled. The task’s success condition is achieved upon entering the dungeon.

Relevant Achievements: ENTER_DUNGEON

Completed Achievements: None

World:
- Player: Starts on floor 0 (Overworld). Inventory: {"wood_sword": 1}. Attributes default (1/1/1). No other initial items.
- Map:
  - Set floor 0 monster kill count to 0 using `builder.set_monsters_killed(level=0, count=0)` (to override the default open‑ladder state).
  - Manually place one LADDER_DOWN block at coordinates (player_spawn_row + 5, player_spawn_col + 5) on floor 0, on any walkable ground (e.g., grass).
  - Place one melee zombie (mob_name = "melee", type_id = 0) using `builder.add_mobs_randomly_near` with target_pos = the ladder position, min_dist = 2, max_dist = 4, n = 1, on_blocks = [GRASS]. This ensures the zombie is near but not blocking the ladder.
  - No other block modifications; the rest of the overworld terrain is unchanged.
- Mechanics:
  - needs_depletion_multiplier = 0.1   (hunger/thirst/fatigue increase 10× slower, making survival trivial)
  - monsters_killed_to_clear_level = 1  (overrides the default; requires 1 kill on floor 0 to unlock the ladder)
  - melee_spawn_multiplier = 0.0         (no random melee mobs)
  - ranged_spawn_multiplier = 0.0
  - passive_spawn_multiplier = 0.0
  - All other TaskParams at default.</data>
