      <data key="d2">Objective: Learn to fire a bow and kill a skeleton (ranged enemy), building ranged‑combat proficiency for future dungeon progression.
Description: The player begins on floor 0 in a clean, flat grass arena with no survival pressure. A bow and five arrows are already in the inventory. A single skeleton (ranged mob) is placed exactly 4 tiles away, ensuring the player must face it and shoot. All other mob spawns are completely suppressed. The task is terminal when the player successfully fires an arrow (FIRE_BOW) and subsequently defeats the skeleton.
Relevant Achievements: FIRE_BOW, DEFEAT_SKELETON
Completed Achievements: FIND_BOW
World:
- Player: Starting floor 0, inventory {"bow": 1, "arrows": 5}. Player position is the default overworld center at (24, 24). Stats at default (all 1).
- Map:
  - Clear a 15×15 area centered on (24, 24) by filling with BlockType.GRASS (to remove any natural trees, stone, or water that could block arrow flight or movement).
    `builder.fill_area(0, BlockType.GRASS, (16, 16), (32, 32))`
  - Place one skeleton (ranged type) at a random location exactly 4 tiles away from the player (Manhattan distance 4) on grass blocks.
    `builder.add_mobs_randomly_near(rng, 0, "skeleton", MobType.RANGED.value, 1, target_pos=(24,24), min_dist=4, max_dist=4, on_blocks=[BlockType.GRASS])`
- Mechanics:
  - melee_spawn_multiplier = 0.0 (no random melee mobs)
  - ranged_spawn_multiplier = 0.0 (no random ranged mobs)
  - passive_spawn_multiplier = 0.0 (no passive mobs)
  - needs_depletion_multiplier = 0.0 (hunger/thirst/fatigue do not increase, survival pressure removed)
  - All other TaskParams at default.</data>
