      <data key="d2">Objective: Descend to the Dungeon and consume a snail to learn vertical progression.
Description: The agent starts on Floor 0 with a stone pickaxe, stone sword, 5 torches, 5 wood, 5 stone, and 1 wood pickaxe in its inventory, eliminating the need for basic crafting. A ladder down is placed in the tile directly to the right of the player’s spawn. No hostiles are present on any floor; all spawn multipliers are zero. The player must walk onto the ladder and execute DESCEND to reach Floor 1. On Floor 1, three Snails (passive, type_id=2) are spawned within 1–3 cells of the ladder‑up location (which matches the ladder‑down coordinates). The agent must attack a snail (DO action) to collect and automatically consume it, unlocking EAT_SNAIL. Survival needs are set to normal (needs_depletion_multiplier=1.0) so the snail also helps manage hunger after the descent. All other game rules remain at default.
Relevant Achievements: ENTER_DUNGEON, EAT_SNAIL
Completed Achievements: COLLECT_WOOD, MAKE_WOOD_PICKAXE, COLLECT_STONE, MAKE_STONE_PICKAXE
World:
- Player: Starting floor 0; inventory: wood pickaxe (1), stone pickaxe (1), stone sword (1), torches (5), wood (5), stone (5).
- Map: On floor 0, place a LADDER_DOWN block at the cell immediately to the right of the player’s spawn (i.e., spawn row, spawn column + 1), using `place_block(0, BlockType.LADDER_DOWN, (spawn_r, spawn_c+1))`. On floor 1, add 3 Snails (`mob_name="passive", type_id=2`) using `add_mobs_randomly_near(rng, level=1, mob_name="passive", type_id=2, n=3, target_pos=(spawn_r, spawn_c+1), min_dist=1, max_dist=3, on_blocks=[BlockType.GRASS, BlockType.PATH])`. No other block or mob modifications.
- Mechanics: passive_spawn_multiplier = 0.0, melee_spawn_multiplier = 0.0, ranged_spawn_multiplier = 0.0, needs_depletion_multiplier = 1.0; all other TaskParams remain at their defaults.</data>
      <data key="d3">import jax
from craftax.craftax.constants import Achievement, BlockType, ItemType
from craftax.craftax.craftax_state import EnvParams, StaticEnvParams

from minicraftax.craftax_state import EnvState, TaskParams
from minicraftax.tasks.base_task import BaseTask
from minicraftax.world_builder import WorldBuilder


class Env(BaseTask):
    """Objective: Descend to the Dungeon and consume a snail to learn vertical progression.
    Description: The agent starts on Floor 0 with a stone pickaxe, stone sword, 5 torches, 5 wood, 5 stone, and 1 wood pickaxe in its inventory, eliminating the need for basic crafting. A ladder down is placed in the tile directly to the right of the player’s spawn. No hostiles are present on any floor; all spawn multipliers are zero. The player must walk onto the ladder and execute DESCEND to reach Floor 1. On Floor 1, three Snails (passive, type_id=2) are spawned within 1–3 cells of the ladder‑up location (which matches the ladder‑down coordinates). The agent must attack a snail (DO action) to collect and automatically consume it, unlocking EAT_SNAIL. Survival needs are set to normal (needs_depletion_multiplier=1.0) so the snail also helps manage hunger after the descent. All other game rules remain at default.
    Relevant Achievements: ENTER_DUNGEON, EAT_SNAIL
    Completed Achievements: COLLECT_WOOD, MAKE_WOOD_PICKAXE, COLLECT_STONE, MAKE_STONE_PICKAXE
    World:
    - Player: Starting floor 0; inventory: wood pickaxe (1), stone pickaxe (1), stone sword (1), torches (5), wood (5), stone (5).
    - Map: On floor 0, place a LADDER_DOWN block at the cell immediately to the right of the player’s spawn (i.e., spawn row, spawn column + 1), using `place_block(0, BlockType.LADDER_DOWN, (spawn_r, spawn_c+1))`. On floor 1, add 3 Snails (`mob_name="passive", type_id=2`) using `add_mobs_randomly_near(rng, level=1, mob_name="passive", type_id=2, n=3, target_pos=(spawn_r, spawn_c+1), min_dist=1, max_dist=3, on_blocks=[BlockType.GRASS, BlockType.PATH])`. No other block or mob modifications.
    - Mechanics: passive_spawn_multiplier = 0.0, melee_spawn_multiplier = 0.0, ranged_spawn_multiplier = 0.0, needs_depletion_multiplier = 1.0; all other TaskParams remain at their defaults.
    """

    def __init__(self, static_params: StaticEnvParams, params: EnvParams):
        super().__init__(static_params, params)
        self.relevant_achievements = [
            Achievement.ENTER_DUNGEON,
            Achievement.EAT_SNAIL,
        ]
        self.completed_achievements = [
            Achievement.COLLECT_WOOD,
            Achievement.MAKE_WOOD_PICKAXE,
            Achievement.COLLECT_STONE,
            Achievement.MAKE_STONE_PICKAXE,
        ]
        self.label = "ENTER_DUNGEON, EAT_SNAIL"

    def get_task_params(self) -&gt; TaskParams:
        """Return custom parameters for this task."""
        return TaskParams(
            passive_spawn_multiplier=0.0,
            melee_spawn_multiplier=0.0,
            ranged_spawn_multiplier=0.0,
            needs_depletion_multiplier=1.0,
        )

    def generate_world(self, rng: jax.Array) -&gt; EnvState:
        """Generates the world for the task."""
        rng, build_rng, snail_rng = jax.random.split(rng, 3)

        builder = WorldBuilder(build_rng, self.static_params, self.params)

        builder.set_starting_floor(0)

        # Provide inventory: stone pickaxe (2), stone sword (2), torches, wood, stone
        builder.set_player_inventory({
            "pickaxe": 2,   # stone pickaxe (covers completed wood &amp; stone achievements)
            "sword": 2,     # stone sword
            "torches": 5,
            "wood": 5,
            "stone": 5,
        })

        # Spawn position for floor 0
        spawn_r, spawn_c = builder.player_position

        # Place a ladder down item one tile to the right (ladders are items, not blocks)
        builder.item_map = builder.item_map.at[0, spawn_r, spawn_c + 1].set(
            ItemType.LADDER_DOWN.value
        )

        # Get the up‑ladder position on floor 1 (where the player will arrive)
        ladder_up_floor1 = builder.ladders_up[1]

        # Add 3 passive snails near the arrival point
        builder.add_mobs_randomly_near(
            snail_rng,
            level=1,
            mob_name="passive",
            type_id=2,   # Snail
            n=3,
            target_pos=ladder_up_floor1,
            min_dist=1,
            max_dist=3,
            on_blocks=[BlockType.GRASS, BlockType.PATH],
        )

        return builder.build(rng)</data>
