      <data key="d2">Objective: Teach the agent to enter the dungeon by using the `DESCEND` action on a down-ladder, unlocking the transition to floor 1.

Description: This task isolates the single new skill of descending a ladder to a new floor. The agent starts on the overworld (floor 0) at coordinates (31, 31). A ladder-down block is placed exactly at (31, 27), four tiles to the left, ensuring a short and unobstructed walk. All hostile and passive mob spawns are suppressed (spawn multipliers set to 0.0) so no combat encounters can occur, and any pre-existing mobs will despawn if the agent moves away. Survival needs (hunger, thirst, fatigue) operate at their normal rate, but the trivial navigation distance means the agent can reach the ladder well before any stat depletion becomes a problem. No starting inventory or tools are provided, so the agent cannot craft, mine, or fight. The episode terminates successfully as soon as the agent performs a `DESCEND` action while standing on the ladder-down and changes floor.

Relevant Achievements:
- ENTER_DUNGEON

Completed Achievements:
- None

World:
- Player: Starts on floor 0 at coordinates (31, 31) with default starting attributes (all stats 9/9, no inventory, no tools, no enchantments, no spells, no armour).
- Map:
  * Place one `Ladder Down` block at (31, 27) on floor 0 using `builder.place_block(0, BlockType.LADDER_DOWN, (31, 27))`.
  * No other manual block or mob modifications.
- Mechanics:
  * `melee_spawn_multiplier = 0.0`
  * `ranged_spawn_multiplier = 0.0`
  * `passive_spawn_multiplier = 0.0`
  * `needs_depletion_multiplier = 1.0`
  * `health_recover_multiplier = 1.0`
  * `mob_damage_multiplier = 1.0` (default, irrelevant due to no mobs)
  * `monsters_killed_to_clear_level` for floor 0 = 0 (default, already open)
  * All other `TaskParams` remain at their default settings.</data>
