      <data key="d2">Objective: Defeat an Orc Soldier in the dungeon with a stone sword while survival needs are suspended.
Description: The agent starts on Floor 1 (the dungeon) with a stone sword. One Orc Soldier (melee, type_id=2) is placed within 3–6 tiles (Manhattan distance) of the start. All mob spawning multipliers are set to 0.0, so no other enemies appear. Survival needs (hunger, thirst, fatigue) are disabled by setting needs_depletion_multiplier to 0.0; the player’s food, drink, and energy remain at maximum indefinitely, ensuring health regeneration conditions are always met. Health recover and loss multipliers remain at 1.0. The task is a success the moment the Orc Soldier is defeated. No other achievements are required.
Relevant Achievements: DEFEAT_ORC_SOLIDER
Completed Achievements: MAKE_STONE_SWORD, ENTER_DUNGEON
World:
- Player: Starts on floor 1. Inventory: `{"sword": 2}` (stone sword). MAKE_STONE_SWORD and ENTER_DUNGEON achievements completed.
- Map:
  - Add one Orc Soldier (melee mob, mob_name "Orc Soldier", type_id=2) randomly within 3–6 Manhattan distance of the player start position.
  - No other initial mobs, no block modifications.
- Mechanics:
  - needs_depletion_multiplier = 0.0
  - melee_spawn_multiplier = 0.0
  - ranged_spawn_multiplier = 0.0
  - passive_spawn_multiplier = 0.0
  - All other TaskParams at default (mob_health_multiplier = 1.0, mob_damage_multiplier = 1.0, health_recover_multiplier = 1.0, health_loss_multiplier = 1.0, etc.).</data>
      <data key="d3">import jax
from craftax.craftax.constants import Achievement, BlockType
from craftax.craftax.craftax_state import EnvParams, StaticEnvParams

from minicraftax.craftax_state import EnvState, TaskParams
from minicraftax.tasks.base_task import BaseTask
from minicraftax.world_builder import WorldBuilder


class Env(BaseTask):
    """Objective: Defeat an Orc Soldier in the dungeon with a stone sword while survival needs are suspended.
    Description: The agent starts on Floor 1 (the dungeon) with a stone sword. One Orc Soldier (melee, type_id=2) is placed within 3–6 tiles (Manhattan distance) of the start. All mob spawning multipliers are set to 0.0, so no other enemies appear. Survival needs (hunger, thirst, fatigue) are disabled by setting needs_depletion_multiplier to 0.0; the player’s food, drink, and energy remain at maximum indefinitely, ensuring health regeneration conditions are always met. Health recover and loss multipliers remain at 1.0. The task is a success the moment the Orc Soldier is defeated. No other achievements are required.
    Relevant Achievements: DEFEAT_ORC_SOLIDER
    Completed Achievements: MAKE_STONE_SWORD, ENTER_DUNGEON
    World:
    - Player: Starts on floor 1. Inventory: `{"sword": 2}` (stone sword). MAKE_STONE_SWORD and ENTER_DUNGEON achievements completed.
    - Map:
      - Add one Orc Soldier (melee mob, mob_name "Orc Soldier", type_id=2) randomly within 3–6 Manhattan distance of the player start position.
      - No other initial mobs, no block modifications.
    - Mechanics:
      - needs_depletion_multiplier = 0.0
      - melee_spawn_multiplier = 0.0
      - ranged_spawn_multiplier = 0.0
      - passive_spawn_multiplier = 0.0
      - All other TaskParams at default (mob_health_multiplier = 1.0, mob_damage_multiplier = 1.0, health_recover_multiplier = 1.0, health_loss_multiplier = 1.0, etc.).
    """

    def __init__(self, static_params: StaticEnvParams, params: EnvParams):
        super().__init__(static_params, params)
        self.relevant_achievements = [Achievement.DEFEAT_ORC_SOLIDER]
        self.completed_achievements = [
            Achievement.MAKE_STONE_SWORD,
            Achievement.ENTER_DUNGEON,
        ]
        self.label = "DEFEAT_ORC_SOLIDER"

    def get_task_params(self) -&gt; TaskParams:
        """Return custom parameters for this task."""
        return TaskParams(
            needs_depletion_multiplier=0.0,
            melee_spawn_multiplier=0.0,
            ranged_spawn_multiplier=0.0,
            passive_spawn_multiplier=0.0,
        )

    def generate_world(self, rng: jax.Array) -&gt; EnvState:
        """Generates the world for the task."""
        rng, build_rng, mob_rng = jax.random.split(rng, 3)

        builder = WorldBuilder(build_rng, self.static_params, self.params)

        builder.set_starting_floor(1)
        builder.set_player_inventory({"sword": 2})  # 2 = stone sword

        # Place one Orc Soldier (melee type_id=2) near the player
        builder.add_mobs_randomly_near(
            mob_rng,
            level=1,
            mob_name="melee",
            type_id=2,      # Orc Soldier
            n=1,
            target_pos=builder.player_position,
            min_dist=3,
            max_dist=6,
            # Default on_blocks includes PATH, which works for dungeon floor 1
        )

        return builder.build(rng)</data>
