      <data key="d10">**Global Bottleneck Hypothesis (Objective Signal):**
The ORIGINAL Craftax profile shows the agent can enter the dungeon (73.38% ENTER_DUNGEON) but struggles severely with combat on floor 1: DEFEAT_ORC_SOLIDER at 16.23% and DEFEAT_ORC_MAGE at 0.65%. This combat gate is a key progression blocker, because clearing floor 1 requires defeating these hostile mobs. Improving orc combat directly transfers to surviving and progressing in the dungeon, unlocking deeper floors and resources.

**Parent Capability Frontier:**
The trained task ("descend to dungeon with stone tools") demonstrates the agent can reliably reach the ladder and descend (ENTER_DUNGEON SR 79%) with stone pick/sword, some torches, and no combat prerequisite. Thus the agent can navigate the overworld, locate the ladder, and perform the descend action under benign conditions. We can compress away overworld navigation and initial crafting to focus entirely on the next challenge: fighting an orc soldier in the dungeon environment.

**Diagnosis: Local vs Global:**
Local performance on the trained task showed high ENTER_DUNGEON (79%) and many accidental skills (collect iron, place furnace, make iron tools). These side skills are already decent globally or emerging, so they do not need explicit attention. The critical gap is the missing dungeon combat. The low global DEFEAT_ORC_SOLIDER despite decent zombie/skeleton combat globally (77%/69%) suggests that the orc's higher stats (health 7, damage 3) and possibly the dungeon's layout/lighting are the new challenge. This is a high-value expansion target.

**Evolution Choice: EXPAND.**
We apply one main forward dependency: learn to defeat an Orc Soldier in the dungeon. This is a thin-slice expansion beyond the parent frontier (enter dungeon). We start the agent on floor 1 with the same stone tools, provide a single orc soldier nearby, suppress all other spawns, and lighten survival pressure to keep focus.

**Scaffolding &amp; Backtracking Avoidance:**
Initial state places the agent on Floor 1 at the up-ladder spawn with inventory that matches a competent arrival from the parent task (stone sword, stone pickaxe, torches). All prerequisites for reaching that point (enter dungeon, stone crafting) are marked as completed achievements, so no backtracking is required. A torch is placed at spawn to avoid darkness penalty, and an orc soldier is spawned within a few steps, guaranteeing a learnable encounter.

**Final Consistency Check:**
- Trained Task Relevant Achievements: [ENTER_DUNGEON]
- New Task Relevant Achievements: [DEFEAT_ORC_SOLIDER]
- “One-main-change” check: YES – we added exactly one new dependency (defeat a specific dungeon melee mob) and removed all other pressures (no other spawns, slower needs).
- Backtracking check: YES – the agent starts on floor 1 with the necessary equipment and the achievements that would already have been earned to get there; no need to return to earlier floors.</data>
