      <data key="d2">Objective: Defeat an Orc Soldier in the dungeon with a stone sword while survival needs are fully active.
Description: The agent starts on Floor 1 (the dungeon) with a stone sword. One Orc Soldier (melee, type_id=2) is placed within 3–6 tiles (Manhattan distance) of the start. Two Snail passive mobs (type_id=2) are placed within 2–5 tiles of the start to provide an immediate food source. Survival needs (hunger, thirst, fatigue) are fully enabled with needs_depletion_multiplier = 1.0. Passive mob spawning is enabled at 1.0 so additional snails can spawn naturally on the dungeon floor. Melee and ranged hostile spawning remain at 0.0 so the initial Orc Soldier is the only combat threat. Health recovery and loss multipliers are at default (1.0), meaning the agent will regenerate health when all needs are met and lose health when starving or dehydrated. The dungeon's natural fountain generation provides water sources. The task is a success the moment the Orc Soldier is defeated. No other achievements are required for termination.
Relevant Achievements: DEFEAT_ORC_SOLIDER
Completed Achievements: MAKE_STONE_SWORD, ENTER_DUNGEON
World:
- Player: Starts on floor 1. Inventory: `{"sword": 2}` (stone sword). MAKE_STONE_SWORD and ENTER_DUNGEON achievements completed.
- Map:
  - Add one Orc Soldier (melee mob, mob_name "Orc Soldier", type_id=2) randomly within 3–6 Manhattan distance of the player start position.
  - Add two Snail passive mobs (passive mob, mob_name "Snail", type_id=2) randomly within 2–5 Manhattan distance of the player start position, on valid walkable terrain (e.g., PATH blocks).
  - No block modifications.
- Mechanics:
  - needs_depletion_multiplier = 1.0
  - passive_spawn_multiplier = 1.0
  - melee_spawn_multiplier = 0.0
  - ranged_spawn_multiplier = 0.0
  - All other TaskParams at default (mob_health_multiplier = 1.0, mob_damage_multiplier = 1.0, health_recover_multiplier = 1.0, health_loss_multiplier = 1.0, mana_recover_multiplier = 1.0, etc.).</data>
      <data key="d3">import jax
from craftax.craftax.constants import Achievement, BlockType
from craftax.craftax.craftax_state import EnvParams, StaticEnvParams

from minicraftax.craftax_state import EnvState, TaskParams
from minicraftax.tasks.base_task import BaseTask
from minicraftax.world_builder import WorldBuilder


class Env(BaseTask):
    """Objective: Defeat an Orc Soldier in the dungeon with a stone sword while survival needs are fully active.
    Description: The agent starts on Floor 1 (the dungeon) with a stone sword. One Orc Soldier (melee, type_id=2) is placed within 3–6 tiles (Manhattan distance) of the start. Two Snail passive mobs (type_id=2) are placed within 2–5 tiles of the start to provide an immediate food source. Survival needs (hunger, thirst, fatigue) are fully enabled with needs_depletion_multiplier = 1.0. Passive mob spawning is enabled at 1.0 so additional snails can spawn naturally on the dungeon floor. Melee and ranged hostile spawning remain at 0.0 so the initial Orc Soldier is the only combat threat. Health recovery and loss multipliers are at default (1.0), meaning the agent will regenerate health when all needs are met and lose health when starving or dehydrated. The dungeon's natural fountain generation provides water sources. The task is a success the moment the Orc Soldier is defeated. No other achievements are required for termination.
    Relevant Achievements: DEFEAT_ORC_SOLIDER
    Completed Achievements: MAKE_STONE_SWORD, ENTER_DUNGEON
    World:
    - Player: Starts on floor 1. Inventory: `{"sword": 2}` (stone sword). MAKE_STONE_SWORD and ENTER_DUNGEON achievements completed.
    - Map:
      - Add one Orc Soldier (melee mob, mob_name "Orc Soldier", type_id=2) randomly within 3–6 Manhattan distance of the player start position.
      - Add two Snail passive mobs (passive mob, mob_name "Snail", type_id=2) randomly within 2–5 Manhattan distance of the player start position, on valid walkable terrain (e.g., PATH blocks).
      - No block modifications.
    - Mechanics:
      - needs_depletion_multiplier = 1.0
      - passive_spawn_multiplier = 1.0
      - melee_spawn_multiplier = 0.0
      - ranged_spawn_multiplier = 0.0
      - All other TaskParams at default (mob_health_multiplier = 1.0, mob_damage_multiplier = 1.0, health_recover_multiplier = 1.0, health_loss_multiplier = 1.0, mana_recover_multiplier = 1.0, etc.).
    """

    def __init__(self, static_params: StaticEnvParams, params: EnvParams):
        super().__init__(static_params, params)
        self.relevant_achievements = [Achievement.DEFEAT_ORC_SOLIDER]
        self.completed_achievements = [
            Achievement.MAKE_STONE_SWORD,
            Achievement.ENTER_DUNGEON,
        ]
        self.label = "DEFEAT_ORC_SOLIDER"

    def get_task_params(self) -&gt; TaskParams:
        """Return custom parameters for this task."""
        return TaskParams(
            passive_spawn_multiplier=1.0,
            melee_spawn_multiplier=0.0,
            ranged_spawn_multiplier=0.0,
            needs_depletion_multiplier=1.0,
        )

    def generate_world(self, rng: jax.Array) -&gt; EnvState:
        """Generates the world for the task."""
        rng, build_rng, orc_rng, snail_rng = jax.random.split(rng, 4)

        builder = WorldBuilder(build_rng, self.static_params, self.params)

        builder.set_starting_floor(1)
        builder.set_player_inventory({"sword": 2})  # stone sword

        # Place 1 Orc Soldier near the player on level 1
        builder.add_mobs_randomly_near(
            orc_rng,
            level=1,
            mob_name="melee",
            type_id=2,  # Orc Soldier
            n=1,
            target_pos=builder.player_position,
            min_dist=3,
            max_dist=6,
            on_blocks=[BlockType.PATH],
        )

        # Place 2 Snails near the player on level 1
        builder.add_mobs_randomly_near(
            snail_rng,
            level=1,
            mob_name="passive",
            type_id=2,  # Snail
            n=2,
            target_pos=builder.player_position,
            min_dist=2,
            max_dist=5,
            on_blocks=[BlockType.PATH],
        )

        return builder.build(rng)</data>
