      <data key="d2">Objective: Chain the early‐game crafting sequence of making a stone sword, entering the Dungeon, and defeating an Orc Mage – teaching the agent to handle a ranged threat that kites and shoots projectiles.

Description:
The agent starts on floor 0 (Overworld) with an empty inventory and default stats (STR 1, DEX 1, INT 1; all needs maxed). No hostile mobs spawn anywhere (melee and ranged spawn multipliers set to 0.0). The overworld uses the standard generation rules for trees, stone, coal, iron, and other resources. The dungeon (floor 1) contains exactly one Orc Mage (ranged, type_id=2) placed randomly at a Manhattan distance of 1–3 from the floor’s up‑ladder, guaranteeing a quick ranged encounter after descending. The ladder down on floor 0 is open from the start (0 kills required). The episode terminates in success only when all three achievements – `MAKE_STONE_SWORD`, `ENTER_DUNGEON`, and `DEFEAT_ORC_MAGE` – have been obtained. The task provides exactly one learning pressure: the agent must craft a stone sword, descend, and then close distance on a kiting ranged mob to defeat it with melee, while dodging incoming projectiles.

Relevant Achievements: MAKE_STONE_SWORD, ENTER_DUNGEON, DEFEAT_ORC_MAGE
Completed Achievements: (none)
