      <data key="d8">25</data>
      <data key="d10">1) Global Bottleneck Hypothesis:
The agent can reliably descend into the dungeon (global ENTER_DUNGEON 70.67%, trained task 83.54%), but its combat against dungeon mobs is fragile: global defeat_orc_solider 37.68% and defeat_orc_mage 8.55%. Entering Gnome Mines (floor 2) is the next critical progression gate, requiring clearing floor 1. Improving dungeon combat (melee vs. orcs, survival against mages) will directly raise downstream progression.

2) Parent Capability Frontier:
The trained task proves the agent can navigate the overworld, fight basic zombies/skeletons, and use stone gear to enter the dungeon. It can already gather wood/stone and sometimes craft iron tools. These prerequisites can be compressed: start the agent already on floor 1 with a stone sword and stone pickaxe, so training focuses on dungeon combat and descent rather than overworld backtracking.

3) Diagnosis: Local vs Global:
Task‑specific performance shows strong combat against overworld mobs (defeat_zombie 52%, defeat_skeleton 49%) and high dungeon entry (83.54%). Globally, dungeon mob fights are weak. The agent’s global high combat on overworld mobs suggests local success is genuine, but dungeon enemies (orc soldier/ mage) are a new threat needing focused practice. The agent also has low global eat_snail (49%) and open_chest (67%), but combat is the primary bottleneck for clearing the dungeon. We target combat first.

4) Evolution Choice – Expand:
One forward dependency: “dungeon clearing and descent” builds directly on the parent’s overworld‑to‑dungeon transition. To make it learnable, we scaffold by reducing the kill requirement to 4 and heavily limiting ranged enemies (mages) via low spawn multiplier, while keeping melee spawn moderate. This gives the agent manageable encounters with orc soldiers (which are weak globally) and only occasional mages, creating a thin‑slice beyond the parent frontier.

5) Scaffolding &amp; Backtracking Avoidance:
Start the agent on floor 1 (dungeon) with a stone sword and stone pickaxe, removing the need to craft or go back to the overworld. The ladder‑down requirement is lowered to 4 kills; ranged spawn multiplier = 0.1 makes mages rare. Completed achievements include ENTER_DUNGEON, MAKE_STONE_SWORD, MAKE_STONE_PICKAXE (all implicit from the start state). No backtracking to floor 0 is needed.

6) Final Consistency Check:
- Trained Task Relevant Achievements: ENTER_DUNGEON
- New Task Relevant Achievements: ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES
- New Task Completed Achievements: ENTER_DUNGEON, MAKE_STONE_SWORD, MAKE_STONE_PICKAXE
- One‑main‑change: Yes, added floor‑1 clearing with reduced kill requirement + spawn‑rate tuning; still one primary dependency (dungeon descent).
- Backtracking: Yes, start on floor 1 with stone gear avoids any need to return to overworld.</data>
