      <data key="d0">B</data>
      <data key="d1">generated</data>
      <data key="d2">Objective: Learn to fight both melee and ranged dungeon enemies by defeating an Orc Soldier and an Orc Mage in the Dungeon.

Description:
The agent starts on floor 1 (Dungeon) with a Stone Sword already equipped, all stats at default (STR 1, DEX 1, INT 1), and all needs (health, food, drink, energy, mana) fully maxed. No hostile mobs spawn anywhere – both `melee_spawn_multiplier` and `ranged_spawn_multiplier` are set to 0.0. Exactly two enemies are placed near the starting up‑ladder: one Orc Soldier (`mob_name="melee"`, `type_id=2`) and one Orc Mage (`mob_name="ranged"`, `type_id=2`), each located randomly within a Manhattan distance of 1 to 3 from the up‑ladder position on floor 1. The rest of the floor retains standard dungeon generation (rooms, corridors, chests, fountains). The episode terminates successfully only when both `DEFEAT_ORC_SOLIDER` and `DEFEAT_ORC_MAGE` are obtained. Because the agent is already in the dungeon and already possesses a stone sword, the achievements `MAKE_STONE_SWORD` and `ENTER_DUNGEON` are treated as completed and do not need to be re‑achieved during the task.

Relevant Achievements: DEFEAT_ORC_SOLIDER, DEFEAT_ORC_MAGE
Completed Achievements: MAKE_STONE_SWORD, ENTER_DUNGEON
World:
- Player: Start on floor 1. Inventory contains a stone sword (sword level 2). All player stats and needs are at their default maximums (health 9, food 9, drink 9, energy 9, mana 9).
- Map: On floor 1, add exactly two mobs: one Orc Soldier (`mob_name="melee"`, `type_id=2`) and one Orc Mage (`mob_name="ranged"`, `type_id=2`), each placed randomly within 1–3 Manhattan distance of the up‑ladder position.
- Mechanics:
    * `melee_spawn_multiplier = 0.0`
    * `ranged_spawn_multiplier = 0.0`
    * All other `TaskParams` are left at their default values (including `monsters_killed_to_clear_level` unchanged).</data>
      <data key="d3">import jax
from craftax.craftax.constants import Achievement, BlockType
from craftax.craftax.craftax_state import EnvParams, StaticEnvParams

from minicraftax.craftax_state import EnvState, TaskParams
from minicraftax.tasks.base_task import BaseTask
from minicraftax.world_builder import WorldBuilder


class Env(BaseTask):
    """Objective: Learn to fight both melee and ranged dungeon enemies by defeating an Orc Soldier and an Orc Mage in the Dungeon.

    Description:
    The agent starts on floor 1 (Dungeon) with a Stone Sword already equipped, all stats at default (STR 1, DEX 1, INT 1), and all needs (health, food, drink, energy, mana) fully maxed. No hostile mobs spawn anywhere – both `melee_spawn_multiplier` and `ranged_spawn_multiplier` are set to 0.0. Exactly two enemies are placed near the starting up‑ladder: one Orc Soldier (`mob_name="melee"`, `type_id=2`) and one Orc Mage (`mob_name="ranged"`, `type_id=2`), each located randomly within a Manhattan distance of 1 to 3 from the up‑ladder position on floor 1. The rest of the floor retains standard dungeon generation (rooms, corridors, chests, fountains). The episode terminates successfully only when both `DEFEAT_ORC_SOLIDER` and `DEFEAT_ORC_MAGE` are obtained. Because the agent is already in the dungeon and already possesses a stone sword, the achievements `MAKE_STONE_SWORD` and `ENTER_DUNGEON` are treated as completed and do not need to be re‑achieved during the task.

    Relevant Achievements: DEFEAT_ORC_SOLIDER, DEFEAT_ORC_MAGE
    Completed Achievements: MAKE_STONE_SWORD, ENTER_DUNGEON
    World:
    - Player: Start on floor 1. Inventory contains a stone sword (sword level 2). All player stats and needs are at their default maximums (health 9, food 9, drink 9, energy 9, mana 9).
    - Map: On floor 1, add exactly two mobs: one Orc Soldier (`mob_name="melee"`, `type_id=2`) and one Orc Mage (`mob_name="ranged"`, `type_id=2`), each placed randomly within 1–3 Manhattan distance of the up‑ladder position.
    - Mechanics:
        * `melee_spawn_multiplier = 0.0`
        * `ranged_spawn_multiplier = 0.0`
        * All other `TaskParams` are left at their default values (including `monsters_killed_to_clear_level` unchanged).
    """

    def __init__(self, static_params: StaticEnvParams, params: EnvParams):
        super().__init__(static_params, params)
        self.relevant_achievements = [
            Achievement.DEFEAT_ORC_SOLIDER,
            Achievement.DEFEAT_ORC_MAGE,
        ]
        self.completed_achievements = [
            Achievement.MAKE_STONE_SWORD,
            Achievement.ENTER_DUNGEON,
        ]
        self.label = "DEFEAT_ORC_SOLIDER, DEFEAT_ORC_MAGE"

    def get_task_params(self) -&gt; TaskParams:
        """Return custom parameters for this task."""
        return TaskParams(
            melee_spawn_multiplier=0.0,
            ranged_spawn_multiplier=0.0,
        )

    def generate_world(self, rng: jax.Array) -&gt; EnvState:
        """Generates the world for the task."""
        rng, build_rng = jax.random.split(rng)
        builder = WorldBuilder(build_rng, self.static_params, self.params)

        builder.set_starting_floor(1)                         # Start on floor 1 (Dungeon)
        builder.set_player_inventory({"sword": 2})            # Stone sword

        # Split remaining rng for mob placements
        rng, melee_rng, ranged_rng = jax.random.split(rng, 3)

        # Place Orc Soldier (melee, type_id=2) near the up‑ladder (which is player_position now)
        builder.add_mobs_randomly_near(
            melee_rng,
            level=1,
            mob_name="melee",
            type_id=2,                # Orc Soldier
            n=1,
            target_pos=builder.player_position,
            min_dist=1,
            max_dist=3,
            on_blocks=[BlockType.PATH],
        )

        # Place Orc Mage (ranged, type_id=2)
        builder.add_mobs_randomly_near(
            ranged_rng,
            level=1,
            mob_name="ranged",
            type_id=2,                # Orc Mage
            n=1,
            target_pos=builder.player_position,
            min_dist=1,
            max_dist=3,
            on_blocks=[BlockType.PATH],
        )

        return builder.build(rng)</data>
