      <data key="d10">1) Global Bottleneck Hypothesis (Objective Signal):  
The global profile shows ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES at a mere 0.98%, indicating that the agent almost never manages to clear the dungeon floor and descend. This is a critical progression gate; entering floor 2 unlocks new mobs, ores (sapphire/ruby), and eventually higher floors. Training the agent to reliably clear Floor 1 and descend will directly address this main-game transition.

2) Parent Capability Frontier (What the parent proves):  
The trained task demonstrates that the agent can, when provided with pre‑crafted iron gear and a bow with arrows, defeat a single Orc Soldier and a single Orc Mage in a controlled, spawn‑free dungeon environment. The prerequisites of mining, smelting, crafting, and finding the bow can all be safely compressed away via the initial state so that training stays forward‑focused.

3) Diagnosis: Local vs Global (Avoid local traps):  
Locally, the agent achieves defeat_orc_solider (84.16%) and defeat_orc_mage (75.37%), with an overall success rate of 66.07%. Globally, these skills stand at 59.21% and 45.95%, respectively; the dungeon entry rate is 86.49%, yet entering the next floor is near zero. The weakness is therefore not individual orc kills but the ability to accumulate enough kills, manage resources and navigation, and then activate the descent. The parent task’s design (no spawns, only two enemies) masks this broader requirement, so we now expose it.

4) Evolution Choice (Persist / Simplify / Expand / Vary):  
We choose EXPAND: one thin‑slice forward dependency beyond the parent frontier. By enabling normal spawns of Orc Soldiers and Orc Mages and setting a clear‑requirement (kill 6 hostiles) before descending, we force the agent to handle multiple combats, conserve ammunition, and explore the floor for the ladder down. This directly targets the ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES global bottleneck while reusing proven combat capabilities.

5) Scaffolding &amp; Backtracking Avoidance (Start‑state design):  
The agent begins on Floor 1 (dungeon) already equipped with iron sword, bow, 20 arrows, and one iron armour piece; all needs are full. Because we start on the dungeon floor, ENTER_DUNGEON is already satisfied and moved to Completed Achievements. No backtracking to Floor 0 is required. The inventory and gear mirror a competent player who has arrived at Floor 1 normally, so training focuses purely on clearing and descending.

6) Final Consistency Check:  
- Trained Task Relevant Achievements: DEFEAT_ORC_SOLIDER, DEFEAT_ORC_MAGE  
- New Task Relevant Achievements: DEFEAT_ORC_SOLIDER, DEFEAT_ORC_MAGE, ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES  
- New Task Completed Achievements: COLLECT_WOOD, PLACE_TABLE, COLLECT_STONE, COLLECT_COAL, COLLECT_IRON, MAKE_WOOD_PICKAXE, MAKE_WOOD_SWORD, MAKE_STONE_PICKAXE, MAKE_STONE_SWORD, MAKE_IRON_SWORD, MAKE_IRON_ARMOUR, PLACE_FURNACE, ENTER_DUNGEON, FIND_BOW, MAKE_ARROW, FIRE_BOW  
- “One‑main‑change” check: Did you make only one primary change (frontier expansion OR scaffolding OR executional difficulty)? [YES] – the single frontier expansion is the requirement to kill multiple spawned orcs and then descend.  
- Backtracking check: Does the task avoid requiring earlier‑floor crafting for basic prerequisites unless intended? [YES] – all essential gear is provided upfront; no need to revisit Floor 0.</data>
