      <data key="d2">Objective: Clear the Dungeon floor of multiple hostile mobs before descending to the Gnomish Mines.

Description: The agent begins on Floor 1 (Dungeon) at the up‑ladder position, equipped with an iron sword. The dungeon is generated using the default procedural algorithm; the ladder down to Floor 2 (Gnomish Mines) appears in its normal random location (usually inside a room). The descent gate remains locked until the agent defeats exactly three hostile monsters (melee or ranged) on this level. Once three kills are registered, the agent must navigate to the ladder down and execute the DESCEND action. All game mechanics remain at standard difficulty, except survival needs, which are reduced to 20% of normal to keep the focus on combat and navigation. The task requires no Overworld progression and no crafting; the iron sword is provided, and the Dungeon entry is already counted as complete.

Relevant Achievements: ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES

Completed Achievements: MAKE_IRON_SWORD, ENTER_DUNGEON

World:
- Player: Set starting floor to 1 (Dungeon) via `set_starting_floor(1)`. Inventory: `{"sword": 3}` (iron sword). All other attributes default.
- Map:
  - No manual placement of the ladder—leave the default dungeon generation intact (the ladder‑down will be placed automatically by the dungeon generator).
  - Use `set_monsters_killed(level=1, count=0)` to reset the kill counter for Floor 1.
- Mechanics:
  - monsters_killed_to_clear_level = 3
  - needs_depletion_multiplier = 0.2
  - All other multipliers (spawn, health, damage, recovery) remain at 1.0.
  - All other parameters left at default.</data>
      <data key="d3">import jax
from craftax.craftax.constants import Achievement
from craftax.craftax.craftax_state import EnvParams, StaticEnvParams

from minicraftax.craftax_state import EnvState, TaskParams
from minicraftax.tasks.base_task import BaseTask
from minicraftax.world_builder import WorldBuilder


class Env(BaseTask):
    """Objective: Clear the Dungeon floor of multiple hostile mobs before descending to the Gnomish Mines.

    Description: The agent begins on Floor 1 (Dungeon) at the up‑ladder position, equipped with an iron sword. The dungeon is generated using the default procedural algorithm; the ladder down to Floor 2 (Gnomish Mines) appears in its normal random location (usually inside a room). The descent gate remains locked until the agent defeats exactly three hostile monsters (melee or ranged) on this level. Once three kills are registered, the agent must navigate to the ladder down and execute the DESCEND action. All game mechanics remain at standard difficulty, except survival needs, which are reduced to 20% of normal to keep the focus on combat and navigation. The task requires no Overworld progression and no crafting; the iron sword is provided, and the Dungeon entry is already counted as complete.

    Relevant Achievements: ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES

    Completed Achievements: MAKE_IRON_SWORD, ENTER_DUNGEON

    World:
    - Player: Set starting floor to 1 (Dungeon) via `set_starting_floor(1)`. Inventory: `{"sword": 3}` (iron sword). All other attributes default.
    - Map:
      - No manual placement of the ladder—leave the default dungeon generation intact (the ladder‑down will be placed automatically by the dungeon generator).
      - Use `set_monsters_killed(level=1, count=0)` to reset the kill counter for Floor 1.
    - Mechanics:
      - monsters_killed_to_clear_level = 3
      - needs_depletion_multiplier = 0.2
      - All other multipliers (spawn, health, damage, recovery) remain at 1.0.
      - All other parameters left at default.
    """

    def __init__(self, static_params: StaticEnvParams, params: EnvParams):
        super().__init__(static_params, params)
        self.relevant_achievements = [Achievement.ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES]
        self.completed_achievements = [
            Achievement.MAKE_IRON_SWORD,
            Achievement.ENTER_DUNGEON,
        ]
        self.label = "ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES"

    def get_task_params(self) -&gt; TaskParams:
        """Return custom parameters for this task."""
        return TaskParams(
            monsters_killed_to_clear_level=3,
            needs_depletion_multiplier=0.2,
        )

    def generate_world(self, rng: jax.Array) -&gt; EnvState:
        """Generates the world for the task."""
        rng, build_rng = jax.random.split(rng)

        builder = WorldBuilder(build_rng, self.static_params, self.params)

        # Start on floor 1 (Dungeon), with iron sword
        builder.set_starting_floor(1)
        builder.set_player_inventory({"sword": 3})  # iron sword
        # Reset kill counter on floor 1 to 0
        builder.set_monsters_killed(level=1, count=0)

        # Dungeon generation is fully automatic, no further changes needed

        return builder.build(rng)</data>
