    <node id="task_237">
      <data key="d0">desc_generated</data>
      <data key="d1">generated</data>
      <data key="d2">Objective: Learn to explore the natural overworld to gather iron and coal from default ore distribution and craft iron armour, forcing generalization from artificial pre‑placed ores.

Description: The agent begins on the overworld (floor 0) at the default spawn position with a stone pickaxe already in hand (pickaxe tier 2) and with a crafting table and furnace pre‑placed directly next to the starting tile. No other items, tools, or weapons are provided; all natural mob spawning (melee, ranged, passive) is enabled at standard rates. **Crucially, no iron or coal ores are placed artificially**—the world uses the default procedural generation where iron (2% of stone blocks) and coal (3% of stone blocks) appear randomly in stone formations. The agent must therefore explore the overworld, find and mine enough iron (3) and coal (3) from the naturally generated stone terrain, and then craft iron armour using the nearby crafting table and furnace. The task terminates successfully the moment the iron armour piece is crafted. This design eliminates memorisation of fixed ore locations and demands the same open‑ended exploration and prioritisation required in the full Craftax game.

Relevant Achievements: MAKE_IRON_ARMOUR

Completed Achievements: MAKE_WOOD_PICKAXE, MAKE_STONE_PICKAXE, PLACE_TABLE, PLACE_FURNACE

World:
- Player: Starts on floor 0 at position (24,24) (the overworld centre). Inventory contains 1 stone pickaxe (pickaxe tier 2). All other inventory slots empty. Stats: Strength 1, Dexterity 1, Intelligence 1.
- Map:
  - Use place_block to set a CRAFTING_TABLE at (24,25) and a FURNACE at (25,24). These tiles must be empty grass to be valid; ensure they are placed after the default generation.
