      <data key="d2">Objective: Learn to clear the Dungeon floor by defeating a substantial number of hostiles before descending to the Gnomish Mines.

Description: The agent starts on Floor 1 (Dungeon) at the up‑ladder position. It is equipped with an iron sword and a single piece of iron armour (defence +1). The dungeon layout is generated by the default procedural algorithm, with the ladder down to Floor 2 (Gnomish Mines) placed in one of the rooms. The descent gate remains locked until the agent defeats exactly eight hostile monsters (melee or ranged) on this level. Once eight kills are registered, the agent must navigate to the ladder down and execute the DESCEND action. Survival needs are still scaled down to 20% of normal to keep the focus on combat and navigation, and all other mechanics (mob health, damage, spawn rates) remain at standard difficulty. No Overworld progression or crafting is needed; the iron equipment is pre‑supplied and the Dungeon entry is already considered accomplished.

Relevant Achievements: ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES

Completed Achievements: MAKE_IRON_SWORD, MAKE_IRON_ARMOUR, ENTER_DUNGEON

World:
- Player: Starting floor set to 1 via `set_starting_floor(1)`. Inventory via `set_player_inventory({"sword": 3, "armour": 1})`. All attributes default.
- Map:
  - No manual block placement; rely on default dungeon generation for the ladder‑down.
  - Reset the Floor 1 kill counter with `set_monsters_killed(level=1, count=0)`.
- Mechanics:
  - monsters_killed_to_clear_level = 8
  - needs_depletion_multiplier = 0.2
  - All other TaskParams (spawn multipliers, health/damage multipliers, recovery rates) remain 1.0.
  - All other settings left at default.</data>
