    <node id="task_258">
      <data key="d0">B</data>
      <data key="d1">generated</data>
      <data key="d2">Objective: Clear the Dungeon floor of three hostile mobs and descend to the Gnomish Mines while managing standard hunger, thirst, and health depletion.

Description: The agent begins on Floor 1 (Dungeon) at the up‑ladder position, already equipped with an iron sword (inventory: `{"sword": 3}`). The dungeon is generated by the default procedural algorithm, placing the ladder‑down in its usual random location (typically inside a room). The descent remains locked until the agent defeats exactly three hostile monsters (melee or ranged) on this level. The crucial change is that survival needs now deplete at the standard rate (`needs_depletion_multiplier = 1.0`), instead of the previously reduced 0.2. All other game mechanics – mob spawn rates, health/damage multipliers, mana/health recovery/loss – are kept at their default 1.0. The agent must therefore locate and consume food (snails) and water (fountains) to stay alive while seeking and killing three enemies. The task tests sustained combat under authentic survival pressure, directly targeting the global progression bottleneck into the Gnomish Mines.

Relevant Achievements: ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES

Completed Achievements: MAKE_IRON_SWORD, ENTER_DUNGEON

World:
- Player: Starting floor = 1 (via `set_starting_floor(1)`). Inventory: `{"sword": 3}`. All other attributes default.
- Map:
  - No manual block placements; the default dungeon generation is left intact.
  - Kill counter is reset: `set_monsters_killed(level=1, count=0)`.
- Mechanics:
  - monsters_killed_to_clear_level = 3
  - All multipliers (passive/melee/ranged spawn, mob health, mob damage, health recover, health loss, mana recover, needs depletion) remain at 1.0 (standard Craftax).</data>
      <data key="d3">import jax
from craftax.craftax.constants import Achievement, BlockType
from craftax.craftax.craftax_state import EnvParams, StaticEnvParams

from minicraftax.craftax_state import EnvState, TaskParams
from minicraftax.tasks.base_task import BaseTask
from minicraftax.world_builder import WorldBuilder


class Env(BaseTask):
    """Objective: Clear the Dungeon floor of three hostile mobs and descend to the Gnomish Mines while managing standard hunger, thirst, and health depletion.

    Description: The agent begins on Floor 1 (Dungeon) at the up‑ladder position, already equipped with an iron sword (inventory: `{"sword": 3}`). The dungeon is generated by the default procedural algorithm, placing the ladder‑down in its usual random location (typically inside a room). The descent remains locked until the agent defeats exactly three hostile monsters (melee or ranged) on this level. The crucial change is that survival needs now deplete at the standard rate (`needs_depletion_multiplier = 1.0`), instead of the previously reduced 0.2. All other game mechanics – mob spawn rates, health/damage multipliers, mana/health recovery/loss – are kept at their default 1.0. The agent must therefore locate and consume food (snails) and water (fountains) to stay alive while seeking and killing three enemies. The task tests sustained combat under authentic survival pressure, directly targeting the global progression bottleneck into the Gnomish Mines.

    Relevant Achievements: ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES

    Completed Achievements: MAKE_IRON_SWORD, ENTER_DUNGEON

    World:
    - Player: Starting floor = 1 (via `set_starting_floor(1)`). Inventory: `{"sword": 3}`. All other attributes default.
    - Map:
      - No manual block placements; the default dungeon generation is left intact.
      - Kill counter is reset: `set_monsters_killed(level=1, count=0)`.
    - Mechanics:
      - monsters_killed_to_clear_level = 3
      - All multipliers (passive/melee/ranged spawn, mob health, mob damage, health recover, health loss, mana recover, needs depletion) remain at 1.0 (standard Craftax).
    """

    def __init__(self, static_params: StaticEnvParams, params: EnvParams):
        super().__init__(static_params, params)
        self.relevant_achievements = [Achievement.ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES]
        self.completed_achievements = [
            Achievement.MAKE_IRON_SWORD,
            Achievement.ENTER_DUNGEON,
        ]
        self.label = "ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES"

    def get_task_params(self) -&gt; TaskParams:
        """Return custom parameters for this task."""
        return TaskParams(
            monsters_killed_to_clear_level=3,
            passive_spawn_multiplier=1.0,
            melee_spawn_multiplier=1.0,
            ranged_spawn_multiplier=1.0,
            mob_health_multiplier=1.0,
            mob_damage_multiplier=1.0,
            health_recover_multiplier=1.0,
            health_loss_multiplier=1.0,
            mana_recover_multiplier=1.0,
            needs_depletion_multiplier=1.0,
        )

    def generate_world(self, rng: jax.Array) -&gt; EnvState:
        """Generates the world for the task."""
        rng, build_rng = jax.random.split(rng)

        builder = WorldBuilder(build_rng, self.static_params, self.params)

        # Start on floor 1 (Dungeon)
        builder.set_starting_floor(1)

        # Equip iron sword
        builder.set_player_inventory({"sword": 3})  # iron sword

        # Reset kill counter on level 1
        builder.set_monsters_killed(level=1, count=0)

        # No additional block or mob placements; default dungeon generation is used
        return builder.build(rng)</data>
