      <data key="d1">generated</data>
      <data key="d2">Objective: Introduce the agent to descending to the next floor by unlocking the ladder through a short floor‑1 combat encounter and then descending into the Gnomish Mines.

Description: The agent starts on Floor 1 (Dungeon) with a stone sword, stone pickaxe, and a small stash of wood and stone. Two hostile mobs are pre‑placed: one Orc Soldier (melee, type_id=2) and one Orc Mage (ranged, type_id=2), positioned randomly within a few blocks of the player. All spawn multipliers are zero, and the kill requirement to clear the floor is set to 2, so after both kills the ladder down opens. A LADDER_DOWN block is placed randomly 2–5 blocks from the player’s spawn on walkable terrain to ensure easy access after the fight. Mobs deal only 70 % of normal damage (mob_damage_multiplier = 0.7), making the dual‑combat slightly more forgiving and increasing the chance that the agent survives to try the descent. Survival needs are disabled, and all other mechanics are at default values. The episode succeeds when the agent has defeated both orcs and subsequently used the DESCEND action to enter Floor 2 (Gnomish Mines).

Relevant Achievements: DEFEAT_ORC_SOLIDER, DEFEAT_ORC_MAGE, ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES

Completed Achievements: MAKE_WOOD_PICKAXE, MAKE_WOOD_SWORD, MAKE_STONE_PICKAXE, MAKE_STONE_SWORD

World:
- Player: Floor 1 (spawn at the ladder‑up position). Inventory: {"sword": 1, "pickaxe": 1, "wood": 5, "stone": 5}. Base stats (Strength 1, Dexterity 1, Intelligence 1; all bars 9/9). No spells, no enchantments.
- Map:
    - Default Dungeon generation for Floor 1.
    - Place one LADDER_DOWN block using `place_randomly_near` with target_pos = player spawn, min_dist=2, max_dist=5, n=1, on_blocks=[BlockType.PATH] (or any walkable terrain).
    - Place exactly one melee mob Orc Soldier (mob_name="melee", type_id=2) via `add_mobs_randomly_near` with target_pos = player spawn, n=1, min_dist=2, max_dist=8, on any walkable terrain.
    - Place exactly one ranged mob Orc Mage (mob_name="ranged", type_id=2) via `add_mobs_randomly_near` with target_pos = player spawn, n=1, min_dist=2, max_dist=8, on any walkable terrain.
- Mechanics:
    - needs_depletion_multiplier = 0.0
    - melee_spawn_multiplier = 0.0
    - ranged_spawn_multiplier = 0.0
    - passive_spawn_multiplier = 0.0
