      <data key="d10">**Global Bottleneck Hypothesis:**  
The global profile shows ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES SR at only 3.67%, despite a local SR of 57.14% under the scaffolded task. Reaching Gnomish Mines is the critical progression gate for accessing mid‑game floors (Sewers, Vault, etc.) and their associated achievements. A failure to enter floor 2 under original difficulty blocks everything downstream. This is a clear bottleneck – improving the agent’s ability to reliably make that transition under more realistic combat/survival pressure will directly raise global progression.

**Parent Capability Frontier:**  
The trained task proves the agent can, from an empty start, collect wood, stone, coal, iron, craft progressively better tools, craft arrows, find a bow, defeat a mix of Orc Soldiers and Orc Mages, and descend to floor 2 – provided that needs deplete at half rate, mobs deal 75 % damage, and only 6 kills are required. Thus the full sequence from zero to floor 2 is within reach when the environment is forgiving.

**Diagnosis: Local vs Global:**  
Locally the agent achieves high rates on all prerequisite skills (collect_wood 100 %, place_table 100 %, make_stone_sword 86 %, defeat_orc_solider 91 %, etc.), yet overall task SR is only 57 %. The drop may stem from cumulative attrition when needs and damage are higher – the agent still succeeds often but not robustly. Globally, the near‑zero floor‑2 entry suggests that the relaxed mechanics masked fragility in combat efficiency, resource timeliness, or survivability under original damage/hunger rates. These weaknesses must be exposed without adding new dependencies.

**Evolution Choice: Vary**  
We keep the same goal (ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES) but remove the scaffolding that made it easy: restore original survival and combat pressure. This is a single primary change – executional difficulty – that pushes the agent to generalize its existing capability. It does not introduce any new milestones or prerequisites, only demands that the already‑mastered chain be completed under conditions much closer to the original Craftax.

**Scaffolding &amp; Backtracking Avoidance:**  
The agent starts on floor 0 with an empty inventory, exactly as in the original game. No pre‑supplied items, no pre‑unlocked ladders (except the default floor‑0 ladder that is always open). This forces the agent to execute the full crafting‑to‑dungeon‑to‑mines pipeline without shortcuts, but because all prerequisite resources (wood, stone, coal, iron, bow) are acquirable on floors 0 and 1, no backtracking to earlier floors is required. The initial state compresses nothing, matching the standard start.

**Final Consistency Check:**  
- Trained Task Relevant Achievements: [ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES]  
- New Task Relevant Achievements: [ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES]  
- New Task Completed Achievements: (none)  
- One‑main‑change: YES – only survival/combat parameters were raised to default; no new goals or inventory removals.  
- Backtracking check: YES – the agent never needs to return to floor 0 after descending, and all floor‑1 resources are present by default generation.</data>
