      <data key="d2">Objective: Learn to clear enough dungeon enemies to unlock the ladder, then descend to the Gnomish Mines.

Description: The agent starts on floor 1 (the dungeon) with a stone pickaxe, a stone sword, and small stacks of wood (3), stone (3), and coal (2). All mob spawning is disabled (melee_spawn_multiplier, ranged_spawn_multiplier, passive_spawn_multiplier = 0.0) and survival needs are turned off (needs_depletion_multiplier = 0.0), so the agent stays fully fed, hydrated, and rested. Two iron ore blocks are placed within 2–6 Manhattan distance of the player start on any STONE, WALL, or WALL_MOSS block. Three Orc Soldiers (melee mob, mob_name "Orc Soldier", type_id=2) and two Orc Mages (ranged mob, mob_name "Orc Mage", type_id=2) are placed randomly within 5–10 Manhattan distance of the start, ensuring all are reachable on the dungeon level. The ladder-down kill requirement for floor 1 is set to 4 (monsters_killed_to_clear_level = 4). The agent must mine at least one iron block, use the initial resources to place a crafting table and furnace, craft an iron sword, then hunt and kill at least 4 hostile orcs (any combination of the placed soldiers and mages) to unlock the ladder down, and finally descend to floor 2. The episode succeeds only when MAKE_IRON_SWORD and ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES are both achieved.

Relevant Achievements: MAKE_IRON_SWORD, ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES

Completed Achievements: ENTER_DUNGEON, MAKE_STONE_SWORD, MAKE_STONE_PICKAXE

World:
- Player: Starts on floor 1. Inventory: `{"wood": 3, "stone": 3, "coal": 2, "pickaxe": 2, "sword": 2}` (stone pickaxe, stone sword). Completed achievements: ENTER_DUNGEON, MAKE_STONE_SWORD, MAKE_STONE_PICKAXE.
- Map:
  - Place 2 iron ore blocks (BlockType.IRON) randomly within 2–6 Manhattan distance of the player start position, on any blocks of type STONE, WALL, or WALL_MOSS.
  - Add exactly three Orc Soldiers (melee mob, mob_name "Orc Soldier", type_id=2) randomly within 5–10 Manhattan distance of the player start.
  - Add exactly two Orc Mages (ranged mob, mob_name "Orc Mage", type_id=2) randomly within 5–10 Manhattan distance of the player start.
  - No other initial mobs or block modifications.
- Mechanics:
  - monsters_killed_to_clear_level = 4
  - needs_depletion_multiplier = 0.0
  - melee_spawn_multiplier = 0.0
  - ranged_spawn_multiplier = 0.0
  - passive_spawn_multiplier = 0.0
  - All other TaskParams remain at their defaults (mob_health_multiplier = 1.0, mob_damage_multiplier = 1.0, health_recover_multiplier = 1.0, health_loss_multiplier = 1.0, etc.).</data>
      <data key="d3">import jax
from craftax.craftax.constants import Achievement, BlockType
from craftax.craftax.craftax_state import EnvParams, StaticEnvParams

from minicraftax.craftax_state import EnvState, TaskParams
from minicraftax.tasks.base_task import BaseTask
from minicraftax.world_builder import WorldBuilder


class Env(BaseTask):
    """Objective: Learn to clear enough dungeon enemies to unlock the ladder, then descend to the Gnomish Mines.

Description: The agent starts on floor 1 (the dungeon) with a stone pickaxe, a stone sword, and small stacks of wood (3), stone (3), and coal (2). All mob spawning is disabled (melee_spawn_multiplier, ranged_spawn_multiplier, passive_spawn_multiplier = 0.0) and survival needs are turned off (needs_depletion_multiplier = 0.0), so the agent stays fully fed, hydrated, and rested. Two iron ore blocks are placed within 2–6 Manhattan distance of the player start on any STONE, WALL, or WALL_MOSS block. Three Orc Soldiers (melee mob, mob_name "Orc Soldier", type_id=2) and two Orc Mages (ranged mob, mob_name "Orc Mage", type_id=2) are placed randomly within 5–10 Manhattan distance of the start, ensuring all are reachable on the dungeon level. The ladder-down kill requirement for floor 1 is set to 4 (monsters_killed_to_clear_level = 4). The agent must mine at least one iron block, use the initial resources to place a crafting table and furnace, craft an iron sword, then hunt and kill at least 4 hostile orcs (any combination of the placed soldiers and mages) to unlock the ladder down, and finally descend to floor 2. The episode succeeds only when MAKE_IRON_SWORD and ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES are both achieved.

Relevant Achievements: MAKE_IRON_SWORD, ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES

Completed Achievements: ENTER_DUNGEON, MAKE_STONE_SWORD, MAKE_STONE_PICKAXE

World:
- Player: Starts on floor 1. Inventory: `{"wood": 3, "stone": 3, "coal": 2, "pickaxe": 2, "sword": 2}` (stone pickaxe, stone sword). Completed achievements: ENTER_DUNGEON, MAKE_STONE_SWORD, MAKE_STONE_PICKAXE.
- Map:
  - Place 2 iron ore blocks (BlockType.IRON) randomly within 2–6 Manhattan distance of the player start position, on any blocks of type STONE, WALL, or WALL_MOSS.
  - Add exactly three Orc Soldiers (melee mob, mob_name "Orc Soldier", type_id=2) randomly within 5–10 Manhattan distance of the player start.
  - Add exactly two Orc Mages (ranged mob, mob_name "Orc Mage", type_id=2) randomly within 5–10 Manhattan distance of the player start.
  - No other initial mobs or block modifications.
- Mechanics:
  - monsters_killed_to_clear_level = 4
  - needs_depletion_multiplier = 0.0
  - melee_spawn_multiplier = 0.0
  - ranged_spawn_multiplier = 0.0
  - passive_spawn_multiplier = 0.0
  - All other TaskParams remain at their defaults (mob_health_multiplier = 1.0, mob_damage_multiplier = 1.0, health_recover_multiplier = 1.0, health_loss_multiplier = 1.0, etc.).
"""

    def __init__(self, static_params: StaticEnvParams, params: EnvParams):
        super().__init__(static_params, params)
        self.relevant_achievements = [
            Achievement.MAKE_IRON_SWORD,
            Achievement.ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES,
        ]
        self.completed_achievements = [
            Achievement.ENTER_DUNGEON,
            Achievement.MAKE_STONE_SWORD,
            Achievement.MAKE_STONE_PICKAXE,
        ]
        self.label = "MAKE_IRON_SWORD, ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES"

    def get_task_params(self) -&gt; TaskParams:
        """Return custom parameters for this task."""
        return TaskParams(
            passive_spawn_multiplier=0.0,
            melee_spawn_multiplier=0.0,
            ranged_spawn_multiplier=0.0,
            monsters_killed_to_clear_level=4,
            needs_depletion_multiplier=0.0,
        )

    def generate_world(self, rng: jax.Array) -&gt; EnvState:
        """Generates the world for the task."""
        rng, build_rng, iron_rng, melee_rng, ranged_rng = jax.random.split(rng, 5)

        builder = WorldBuilder(build_rng, self.static_params, self.params)

        # Start on floor 1 (dungeon) at the up-ladder position
        builder.set_starting_floor(1)

        # Set starting inventory
        builder.set_player_inventory({
            "wood": 3,
            "stone": 3,
            "coal": 2,
            "pickaxe": 2,       # stone pickaxe
            "sword": 2,         # stone sword
        })

        floor1_spawn = builder.ladders_up[1]  # entry point on floor 1

        # Place 2 iron ore blocks near the player start on STONE, WALL, or WALL_MOSS
        builder.place_randomly_near(
            iron_rng,
            level=1,
            block_type=BlockType.IRON,
            target_pos=floor1_spawn,
            min_dist=2,
            max_dist=6,
            n=2,
            on_blocks=[BlockType.STONE, BlockType.WALL, BlockType.WALL_MOSS],
        )

        # Place three Orc Soldiers (melee, type_id=2) within 5–10 Manhattan distance
        builder.add_mobs_randomly_near(
            melee_rng,
            level=1,
            mob_name="melee",
            type_id=2,
            n=3,
            target_pos=floor1_spawn,
            min_dist=5,
            max_dist=10,
            on_blocks=[BlockType.PATH],
        )

        # Place two Orc Mages (ranged, type_id=2) within 5–10 Manhattan distance
        builder.add_mobs_randomly_near(
            ranged_rng,
            level=1,
            mob_name="ranged",
            type_id=2,
            n=2,
            target_pos=floor1_spawn,
            min_dist=5,
            max_dist=10,
            on_blocks=[BlockType.PATH],
        )

        state = builder.build(rng)

        # Mark pre‑completed achievements as True
        achievements = state.achievements
        for ach in self.completed_achievements:
            achievements = achievements.at[ach.value].set(True)
        state = state.replace(achievements=achievements)

        return state</data>
