    <node id="task_437">
      <data key="d0">desc_generated</data>
      <data key="d1">generated</data>
      <data key="d2">Objective: Teach the agent to reach the Gnomish Mines while managing light survival needs, improving generalisation to the full game.

Description:
This task builds on the overworld‑to‑mines transition by adding a small survival requirement. The agent starts on floor 0 with an empty inventory and the overworld ladder already open (default behaviour). All crafting and combat steps remain the same: it must gather wood, craft a wood pickaxe (MAKE_WOOD_PICKAXE), mine stone, craft a stone sword (MAKE_STONE_SWORD), descend to the dungeon, defeat eight Orcs (Orc Soldiers/Mages) to unlock the floor 1 ladder, and finally descend to floor 2 (ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES). The only mechanical change is that needs are now active at half speed (`needs_depletion_multiplier = 0.5`), forcing the agent to periodically eat, drink, and manage health—skills it already occasionally performs (local eat_cow 94.29%, collect_drink 95.51%). The agent is free to gather any additional resources, but the episode terminates successfully only when it enters the Gnomish Mines.

Relevant Achievements: ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES
Completed Achievements: (none)

World:
- Player: Starts on floor 0. Inventory: completely empty. Armour slots empty. Attributes: strength=1, dexterity=1, intelligence=1. Status bars all 9/9. Enchantments all 0. Learned spells both false.
- Map: The default overworld, dungeon, and all other floors are used with no additional block placements or modifications. The overworld ladder is pre‑unlocked (default `monsters_killed[0] = 10`).
- Mechanics:
  - `needs_depletion_multiplier = 0.5`
  - `monsters_killed_to_clear_level = 8`
  - `mob_damage_multiplier = 1.0`
  - `melee_spawn_multiplier = 1.0`
  - `ranged_spawn_multiplier = 1.0`
  - `passive_spawn_multiplier = 1.0`
  All other `TaskParams` remain at their default values.</data>
