      <data key="d2">Objective: Learn to survive and clear the Gnomish Mines by defeating naturally spawning gnome warriors and archers, and descend to the Sewers.

Description:
The player begins on Floor 2 (Gnomish Mines) at the Ladder Up position, fully refreshed (health 9, food 9, drink 9, energy 9, mana 9) with base attributes (strength=1, dexterity=1, intelligence=1). The initial inventory contains:
- Stone sword (inventory sword level 2)
- Bow (inventory bow level 1)
- 20 arrows
- 15 torches

No other items are provided. The floor’s monster kill count is initialized to 0. The Ladder Down unlocks when the player defeats 5 hostile mobs (`monsters_killed_to_clear_level = 5`). Natural spawning is enabled but dampened: `passive_spawn_multiplier = 0.3` (bats), `melee_spawn_multiplier = 0.7` (gnome warriors), `ranged_spawn_multiplier = 0.7` (gnome archers). Mob health and damage are scaled to 0.9 of default values. Survival pressure is slightly eased: `needs_depletion_multiplier = 0.8`. All other TaskParams remain at default.

The Gnomish Mines are pitch black (default light 0.0), so the player must use torches to navigate the procedurally generated terrain of stone, paths, stalagmites, and lava lakes, and to locate and fight gnomes. The task is considered successful when the player reaches the Ladder Down and executes DESCEND, achieving the `ENTER_SEWERS` achievement.

Relevant Achievements: ENTER_SEWERS

Completed Achievements: ENTER_DUNGEON, ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES, FIND_BOW, MAKE_ARROW, MAKE_TORCH, MAKE_WOOD_SWORD, MAKE_STONE_SWORD

World:
- Player: `builder.set_starting_floor(2)`. Inventory: `{"sword": 2, "bow": 1, "arrows": 20, "torches": 15}`. Stats fully refreshed, attributes 1/1/1.
- Map: No additional block modifications beyond default generation. `builder.set_monsters_killed(level=2, count=0)` to ensure the ladder is initially locked.
- Mechanics: `passive_spawn_multiplier = 0.3`, `melee_spawn_multiplier = 0.7`, `ranged_spawn_multiplier = 0.7`, `monsters_killed_to_clear_level = 5`, `mob_health_multiplier = 0.9`, `mob_damage_multiplier = 0.9`, `needs_depletion_multiplier = 0.8`.</data>
