      <data key="d10">**Justification for New Evolutionary Task:** The agent trained on the parent task to start on Floor 1 with a stone sword, stone pickaxe, bow, arrows, and torches, and beat orcs to unlock the descent to Floor 2. Locally it succeeded 51.85% of the time, but globally ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES remains only 10%. The key bottleneck is that the pre‑supplied ranged weapon and ammunition made combat too easy and prevented the agent from learning to handle the enemies without that gear. Global defeat‑orc‑mage is only 64.19%, suggesting that when a bow is not immediately available the agent struggles. Removing the bow, arrows, and torches forces the agent to rely on melee initially, and to find or craft any ranged capability it wants, thereby improving robust combat on Floor 1 and directly raising the global progression from dungeon entry to Gnomish Mines.

2) **Parent Capability Frontier:** The agent can reliably (≥93%) kill orcs and mages when equipped with a bow and arrows, and it can descend (51.85%). It also demonstrates an ability to explore and gather resources (accidental crafting achievements). The prerequisites of early‑game tool progression are already strong globally, so we can safely compress them.

3) **Diagnosis: Local vs Global:** Local SR 51.85% but global ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES 10% indicates overfitting to the initial ranged kit. Global defeat‑orc‑mage (64.19%) and fire‑bow (86.89%) hint that the agent depends heavily on a pre‑obtained bow. The accidental achievements (collect‑diamond, make‑iron‑sword, etc.) show the agent can already do higher‑tier crafting when allowed to explore, but that is not the core bottleneck.

4) **Evolution Choice:** EXPAND. We keep the same goal (ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES) but remove the bow, arrows, and torches from the starting inventory. This introduces one forward dependency: the agent must either fight exclusively in melee (dealing with mage kiting) or find a bow and craft arrows/torches from resources in the dungeon, thereby strengthening the foundational combat and resourcefulness needed globally. No other parameters are changed.

5) **Scaffolding &amp; Backtracking Avoidance:** Starting on Floor 1 still avoids Floor 0 traversal. The stone sword and pickaxe are consistent with a competent arrival. Completed achievements include the tools that would have been crafted before entering the dungeon. No need to go backwards.

6) **Final Consistency Check:**
   - Trained Task Relevant Achievements: ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES
   - New Task Relevant Achievements: ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES
   - New Task Completed Achievements: COLLECT_WOOD, PLACE_TABLE, MAKE_WOOD_PICKAXE, COLLECT_STONE, MAKE_STONE_PICKAXE, MAKE_STONE_SWORD, ENTER_DUNGEON
   - One‑main‑change: Removed bow/arrows/torches. YES.
   - Backtracking: No requirement to return to Floor 0. YES.</data>
