      <data key="d2">Objective: Increase combat endurance on the Dungeon floor by extending the kill requirement to five enemies, still under standard survival pressure, to prepare for the full game’s 8‑kill gate.

Description: The agent begins on Floor 1 (Dungeon) at the up‑ladder position, holding an iron sword (inventory: `{"sword": 3}`). The dungeon is generated by the default procedural algorithm, placing the ladder‑down in its usual room. The descent to the Gnomish Mines remains locked until the agent defeats exactly five hostile monsters (melee orc soldiers or ranged orc mages) on this level. Survival needs – hunger, thirst, fatigue – deplete at the standard Craftax rate (`needs_depletion_multiplier = 1.0`), forcing the agent to seek out snails and fountains while fighting. All other mechanics (mob spawn rates, health/damage multipliers, recovery rates) are left at their default 1.0. The task directly strengthens the agent’s ability to sustain prolonged combat on the first dungeon floor, the critical bottleneck for entering the Gnomish Mines in the full game.

Relevant Achievements: ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES
Completed Achievements: MAKE_IRON_SWORD, ENTER_DUNGEON

World:
- Player: Starting floor = 1 (via `set_starting_floor(1)`). Inventory: `{"sword": 3}`. All other attributes default.
- Map:
  - No manual block placements; the default dungeon generation is left intact.
  - Kill counter is reset: `set_monsters_killed(level=1, count=0)`.
- Mechanics:
  - `monsters_killed_to_clear_level = 5`
  - All multipliers (passive/melee/ranged spawn, mob health, mob damage, health recover, health loss, mana recover, needs depletion) remain at 1.0 (standard Craftax).</data>
      <data key="d3">import jax
from craftax.craftax.constants import Achievement
from craftax.craftax.craftax_state import EnvParams, StaticEnvParams

from minicraftax.craftax_state import EnvState, TaskParams
from minicraftax.tasks.base_task import BaseTask
from minicraftax.world_builder import WorldBuilder


class Env(BaseTask):
    """Objective: Increase combat endurance on the Dungeon floor by extending the kill requirement to five enemies, still under standard survival pressure, to prepare for the full game’s 8‑kill gate.

Description: The agent begins on Floor 1 (Dungeon) at the up‑ladder position, holding an iron sword (inventory: `{"sword": 3}`). The dungeon is generated by the default procedural algorithm, placing the ladder‑down in its usual room. The descent to the Gnomish Mines remains locked until the agent defeats exactly five hostile monsters (melee orc soldiers or ranged orc mages) on this level. Survival needs – hunger, thirst, fatigue – deplete at the standard Craftax rate (`needs_depletion_multiplier = 1.0`), forcing the agent to seek out snails and fountains while fighting. All other mechanics (mob spawn rates, health/damage multipliers, recovery rates) are left at their default 1.0. The task directly strengthens the agent’s ability to sustain prolonged combat on the first dungeon floor, the critical bottleneck for entering the Gnomish Mines in the full game.

Relevant Achievements: ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES
Completed Achievements: MAKE_IRON_SWORD, ENTER_DUNGEON

World:
- Player: Starting floor = 1 (via `set_starting_floor(1)`). Inventory: `{"sword": 3}`. All other attributes default.
- Map:
  - No manual block placements; the default dungeon generation is left intact.
  - Kill counter is reset: `set_monsters_killed(level=1, count=0)`.
- Mechanics:
  - `monsters_killed_to_clear_level = 5`
  - All multipliers (passive/melee/ranged spawn, mob health, mob damage, health recover, health loss, mana recover, needs depletion) remain at 1.0 (standard Craftax).
"""

    def __init__(self, static_params: StaticEnvParams, params: EnvParams):
        super().__init__(static_params, params)
        self.relevant_achievements = [
            Achievement.ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES,
        ]
        self.completed_achievements = [
            Achievement.MAKE_IRON_SWORD,
            Achievement.ENTER_DUNGEON,
        ]
        self.label = "ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES"

    def get_task_params(self) -&gt; TaskParams:
        """Return custom parameters for this task."""
        return TaskParams(
            monsters_killed_to_clear_level=5,
            needs_depletion_multiplier=1.0,
        )

    def generate_world(self, rng: jax.Array) -&gt; EnvState:
        """Generates the world for the task."""
        rng, build_rng = jax.random.split(rng)

        builder = WorldBuilder(build_rng, self.static_params, self.params)

        # Start on floor 1 (Dungeon) at the up-ladder position
        builder.set_starting_floor(1)

        # Equip starting inventory: iron sword (level 3)
        builder.set_player_inventory({"sword": 3})

        # Reset Dungeon kill counter to zero
        builder.set_monsters_killed(level=1, count=0)

        state = builder.build(rng)

        # Mark completed achievements as True
        achievements = state.achievements
        for ach in self.completed_achievements:
            achievements = achievements.at[ach.value].set(True)
        state = state.replace(achievements=achievements)

        return state</data>
