      <data key="d2">Objective: Learn to independently gather resources, craft a weapon and light source, and then descend into the dungeon to fight orcs and reach the Gnomish Mines.

Description: The agent begins on Floor 0 (Overworld) at the default spawn position. Inventory is completely empty; all attributes are at their base values (strength 1, dexterity 1, intelligence 1). The Overworld contains standard terrain (trees, stone, coal, etc.) but **no hostile mobs** – the `melee_spawn_multiplier` and `ranged_spawn_multiplier` for Floor 0 are set to 0, allowing the agent to gather resources in complete safety. The ladder down to Floor 1 is permanently unlocked (monsters_killed[0] default), so the agent may descend at any time.

On Floor 1 (Dungeon), the environment is fully dark (ambient light 0), with normal spawn rates for Orc Soldiers, Orc Mages, and passive Snails. To advance to Floor 2 (Gnomish Mines), the agent must **kill exactly 5 hostile monsters** (melee or ranged) on Floor 1 and then step onto the ladder down and execute `DESCEND`. The task succeeds only when `ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES` is triggered.

The agent must figure out that it needs to craft at least a stone sword (or better) and torches before entering the Dungeon. Typical required chain on Floor 0: punch trees to obtain wood → craft a Crafting Table (2 wood) → craft a Wood Pickaxe (1 wood) → mine Stone and Coal → craft a Stone Sword (1 wood + 1 stone, at table) and Torches (1 wood + 1 coal, at table). Survival needs are intentionally slowed (`needs_depletion_multiplier = 0.2`) to keep the focus on preparation and combat.

