      <data key="d2">Objective: Learn to mine stone, craft a stone sword on the overworld, then descend into the Dungeon and fight your way to the Gnomish Mines.

Description: The agent begins on Floor 0 (Overworld) at its natural spawn point, with a wood pickaxe (tier 1), 4 torches, and 1 wood already in inventory. A crafting table is pre‑placed directly adjacent to the spawn location (coordinates (24, 25) on the standard 49×49 map). The agent’s first task is to locate a stone block—any of the naturally generated stone blocks on the overworld—mine it using the wood pickaxe to obtain 1 stone, and then use the crafting table to combine the stone and the wood into a stone sword. Once the stone sword is obtained, the agent must explore the overworld to find the ladder down (the Dungeon entrance). Descending will place the agent on Floor 1 (Dungeon), a dark, procedurally generated rooms‑and‑corridors layout with chests, fountains, and corner torches. The agent must place torches to see, kill exactly 5 hostile mobs (Orc Soldiers or Orc Mages) to unlock the ladder to Floor 2 (Gnomish Mines), and finally descend to complete the task. Survival needs (hunger, thirst, fatigue) are slowed to 20% of normal speed to keep the focus on crafting and combat. All mob stats and spawn rates remain at default.

Relevant Achievements: COLLECT_STONE, MAKE_STONE_SWORD, ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES

Completed Achievements: MAKE_WOOD_PICKAXE, MAKE_STONE_PICKAXE, MAKE_WOOD_SWORD, MAKE_STONE_SWORD, MAKE_IRON_SWORD, MAKE_ARROW, MAKE_TORCH, PLACE_TABLE, PLACE_FURNACE, COLLECT_WOOD, COLLECT_STONE, COLLECT_COAL, COLLECT_IRON, ENTER_DUNGEON, PLACE_TORCH

World:
- Player: Start on floor 0 via `set_starting_floor(0)`. Inventory: `{"wood_pickaxe": 1, "torch": 4, "wood": 1}`. Attributes default (strength=1, dexterity=1, intelligence=1).
- Map: 
  - Floor 0: `builder.place_block(0, BlockType.CRAFTING_TABLE, (24, 25))` to position a crafting table immediately next to the player spawn. No other manual modifications; the default overworld generation provides trees, stone, coal, iron, water, sand, lava, zombies, skeletons, cows, and the dungeon ladder.
  - Floor 1: No changes; generated by the standard dungeon algorithm.
  - All other floors remain generated by default but are unused.
- Mechanics:
  - `monsters_killed_to_clear_level = 5` (applies to floor 1 only; floor 0 already requires 0 kills).
  - `needs_depletion_multiplier = 0.2`
  - All other `TaskParams` remain at their default values (spawn multipliers, damage, health, etc.).</data>
