      <data key="d2">Objective: Harden combat-survival integration by entering the Gnomish Mines under moderate survival pressure while maintaining standard combat difficulty.

Description: The agent begins on Floor 0 (Overworld) with empty inventory, max survival stats (food, drink, energy, health, mana = 9/9), and base attributes (STR=1, DEX=1, INT=1). The world uses the default procedural generation for all nine floors. Hostile spawn multipliers are kept at 1.0 (full game rates), so Orc Soldiers and Orc Mages appear with the same frequency as in original Craftax. The kill requirement to clear the Dungeon ladder remains at 8. Survival pressure is increased from the previous task: needs deplete at 0.75× the original rate (`needs_depletion_multiplier = 0.75`) and health recovery rate when needs are met is 1.5× the original (`health_recover_multiplier = 1.5`). All other survival multipliers are at default (1.0). The agent must gather resources, craft weapons and tools, descend into the Dungeon (Floor 1), kill at least 8 hostile monsters (Orc Soldiers, Orc Mages) to open the ladder down, and finally descend to Floor 2 to achieve ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES. The episode ends successfully only upon entering the Gnomish Mines. The moderate survival cost forces the agent to manage food, drink, and health concurrently with combat, reducing overfitting to lenient conditions and improving transfer to the full game.

Relevant Achievements: ENTER_DUNGEON, DEFEAT_ORC_SOLIDER, DEFEAT_ORC_MAGE, ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES
Completed Achievements: (none)

World:
- Player: Starting floor 0; inventory empty; all survival stats (food, drink, energy, health, mana) = 9/9; attributes STR=1, DEX=1, INT=1; no learned spells.
- Map: No modifications; all levels use standard procedural generation.
- Mechanics:
    "melee_spawn_multiplier": 1.0,
    "ranged_spawn_multiplier": 1.0,
    "passive_spawn_multiplier": 1.0,
    "needs_depletion_multiplier": 0.75,
    "health_recover_multiplier": 1.5,
    "monsters_killed_to_clear_level": 8</data>
      <data key="d3">import jax
from craftax.craftax.constants import Achievement
from craftax.craftax.craftax_state import EnvParams, StaticEnvParams

from minicraftax.craftax_state import EnvState, TaskParams
from minicraftax.tasks.base_task import BaseTask
from minicraftax.world_builder import WorldBuilder


class Env(BaseTask):
    """Objective: Harden combat-survival integration by entering the Gnomish Mines under moderate survival pressure while maintaining standard combat difficulty.

Description: The agent begins on Floor 0 (Overworld) with empty inventory, max survival stats (food, drink, energy, health, mana = 9/9), and base attributes (STR=1, DEX=1, INT=1). The world uses the default procedural generation for all nine floors. Hostile spawn multipliers are kept at 1.0 (full game rates), so Orc Soldiers and Orc Mages appear with the same frequency as in original Craftax. The kill requirement to clear the Dungeon ladder remains at 8. Survival pressure is increased from the previous task: needs deplete at 0.75× the original rate (`needs_depletion_multiplier = 0.75`) and health recovery rate when needs are met is 1.5× the original (`health_recover_multiplier = 1.5`). All other survival multipliers are at default (1.0). The agent must gather resources, craft weapons and tools, descend into the Dungeon (Floor 1), kill at least 8 hostile monsters (Orc Soldiers, Orc Mages) to open the ladder down, and finally descend to Floor 2 to achieve ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES. The episode ends successfully only upon entering the Gnomish Mines. The moderate survival cost forces the agent to manage food, drink, and health concurrently with combat, reducing overfitting to lenient conditions and improving transfer to the full game.

Relevant Achievements: ENTER_DUNGEON, DEFEAT_ORC_SOLIDER, DEFEAT_ORC_MAGE, ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES
Completed Achievements: (none)

World:
- Player: Starting floor 0; inventory empty; all survival stats (food, drink, energy, health, mana) = 9/9; attributes STR=1, DEX=1, INT=1; no learned spells.
- Map: No modifications; all levels use standard procedural generation.
- Mechanics:
    "melee_spawn_multiplier": 1.0,
    "ranged_spawn_multiplier": 1.0,
    "passive_spawn_multiplier": 1.0,
    "needs_depletion_multiplier": 0.75,
    "health_recover_multiplier": 1.5,
    "monsters_killed_to_clear_level": 8
"""

    def __init__(self, static_params: StaticEnvParams, params: EnvParams):
        super().__init__(static_params, params)
        self.relevant_achievements = [
            Achievement.ENTER_DUNGEON,
            Achievement.DEFEAT_ORC_SOLIDER,
            Achievement.DEFEAT_ORC_MAGE,
            Achievement.ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES,
        ]
        self.completed_achievements = []  # No pre-completed achievements
        self.label = "ENTER_DUNGEON, DEFEAT_ORC_SOLIDER, DEFEAT_ORC_MAGE, ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES"

    def get_task_params(self) -&gt; TaskParams:
        """Return custom parameters for this task."""
        return TaskParams(
            melee_spawn_multiplier=1.0,
            ranged_spawn_multiplier=1.0,
            passive_spawn_multiplier=1.0,
            needs_depletion_multiplier=0.75,
            health_recover_multiplier=1.5,
            monsters_killed_to_clear_level=8,
        )

    def generate_world(self, rng: jax.Array) -&gt; EnvState:
        """Generates the world for the task."""
        rng, build_rng = jax.random.split(rng)

        builder = WorldBuilder(build_rng, self.static_params, self.params)

        # Start on floor 0 (Overworld) with default spawn and empty inventory
        builder.set_starting_floor(0)

        # No map modifications; completely default generation
        state = builder.build(rng)

        return state</data>
