Description: The agent begins on Floor 1 with a stone sword, stone pickaxe, bow, 10 arrows, and 20 torches – the same equipment that represents a competent overworld run. All survival needs are reactivated (`needs_depletion_multiplier = 1.0`), forcing the agent to manage hunger, thirst, and fatigue while exploring the maze, fighting orcs, and placing torches. To compensate for the added survival burden and maintain a learnable difficulty, the required number of monster kills to unlock the ladder down is reduced from 8 to 4 (`monsters_killed_to_clear_level = 4`). The agent must locate fountains to drink, hunt passive snails for food, and possibly use potions from chests to stay alive, finally locating the ladder down and using the DESCEND action to enter the Gnomish Mines (Floor 2). This task transfers directly to the global game by instilling the necessary survival habits inside the dungeon, closing the gap between high dungeon entry and low mine entry seen in the full Craftax evaluation.

