      <data key="d2">Objective: Learn to chain the transitions from the Overworld to the Gnomish Mines, strengthening the agent’s ability to initiate the descent and then clear the Dungeon under moderate survival pressure.

Description: The agent starts on floor 0 (Overworld) with a wood sword, a wood pickaxe, 10 torches, 6 food, and 6 drink. The ladder down to the Dungeon is already unlocked (the Overworld requires 0 kills), so the agent only needs to navigate to it. The agent must descend to floor 1 (enter the Dungeon), defeat at least eight hostile mobs on that floor to unlock the ladder down, and then descend to floor 2 to reach the Gnomish Mines. Hostile mobs spawn at normal rates on both floors, and survival needs (hunger, thirst, fatigue) accumulate at half the standard speed to give a generous time window. By requiring the agent to begin the chain from the Overworld, this task builds robustness in the full progression from the surface to the mines, while the scaffolded inventory and reduced needs keep the focus on combat and navigation.

Relevant Achievements: ENTER_DUNGEON, ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES  
Completed Achievements: MAKE_WOOD_PICKAXE, MAKE_WOOD_SWORD  

World:
- Player: Starting floor 0. Inventory: `{"wood_sword": 1, "wood_pickaxe": 1, "torch": 10, "food": 6, "drink": 6}`. All other stats default.
- Map: No block modifications (world generates normally).
- Mechanics:
  - needs_depletion_multiplier = 0.5
  - melee_spawn_multiplier = 1.0
  - ranged_spawn_multiplier = 1.0
  - passive_spawn_multiplier = 1.0</data>
