      <data key="d2">Objective: Clear the Gnomish Mines of hostile mobs and descend to the Sewers.

Description: The agent begins on floor 2 (Gnomish Mines) equipped with an iron pickaxe, iron sword, and 20 torches. The mine is pitch‑black, requiring torch placement to navigate. The level generates with stalagmites, lava lakes, abundant coal and iron ore, and occasionally sapphires and rubies. Two new hostile mob types appear: Gnome Warriors (melee, health = 9, damage = 4) and Gnome Archers (ranged, health = 6, damage = 2). Passive bats spawn and can be eaten for food. The agent must explore the procedurally generated caverns, fight and defeat at least 8 hostile mobs to unlock the ladder down, step onto the ladder, and use the DESCEND action to reach floor 3 (Sewers). Survival needs (hunger, thirst, fatigue) deplete at 60% of the normal rate, giving the agent a comfortable window to focus on combat and navigation. No crafting of basic tools is required—the starting inventory provides everything needed to concentrate purely on clearing the floor and advancing.

Relevant Achievements: ENTER_SEWERS

Completed Achievements: MAKE_WOOD_PICKAXE, MAKE_STONE_PICKAXE, MAKE_IRON_PICKAXE, MAKE_WOOD_SWORD, MAKE_STONE_SWORD, MAKE_IRON_SWORD, ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES

World:
- Player:
  - Starting floor 2 (`set_starting_floor(2)`).
  - Default attributes (strength, dexterity, intelligence all 1).
  - Inventory: `set_player_inventory({"pickaxe": 3, "sword": 3, "torch": 20, "wood": 10, "stone": 10})`
  - No enchantments, no learned spells.
- Map: No modifications – floor 2 uses the standard SmoothGen generation for Gnomish Mines (path/stone mix, stalagmites, lava, ores, pitch‑black lighting).
- Mechanics:
  - `monsters_killed_to_clear_level = 8`
  - `needs_depletion_multiplier = 0.6`
  - All other TaskParams remain default (spawn multipliers, mob health/damage, regeneration rates, etc.).</data>
