The agent begins on floor 2 (Gnomish Mines) at the ladder‑up position. It carries the equipment of a player who has competently cleared floor 1: a stone sword, a stone pickaxe, a bow, 15 arrows, and 5 torches. All vital stats are full (health 9, food 9, drink 9, energy 9, mana 9) and attributes are at base (STR 1, DEX 1, INT 1). No armour or enchantments are provided.

Two Gnome Warriors (melee, type_id 1) and one Gnome Archer (ranged, type_id 1) are spawned randomly on floor 2 within a Manhattan distance of 3–8 tiles from the player’s starting position, ensuring immediate combat encounters. Spawn rates for hostiles remain at default (1.0) so additional gnomes may appear over time, keeping pressure high.

Survival needs are drastically slowed (`needs_depletion_multiplier = 0.3`) to remove any starvation or thirst pressure and let the agent concentrate purely on fighting in the pitch‑black mines. The number of kills required to clear the floor is set to 10, preventing accidental ascension and keeping the agent focused on floor 2.

The episode terminates with success as soon as both `DEFEAT_GNOME_WARRIOR` and `DEFEAT_GNOME_ARCHER` achievements are earned. All earlier‑tier crafting achievements that are impossible because the agent already possesses stone tools are listed as completed and should not be pursued.

