      <data key="d2">Objective: Teach the agent to scavenge for coal in the dark dungeon and craft torches/arrows on‑site, so it can reliably navigate and fight before descending to floor 2.

Description: The agent begins on floor 1 with the same basic combat gear as the previous task (stone sword, wood pickaxe, bow) and a small supply of wood (5) and stone (10). However, it receives **no torches, no arrows, and no coal**. The dungeon’s default darkness and hostile mobs (orc soldiers, orc mages) force the agent to seek out coal ore blocks within the dungeon walls, mine them with the wood pickaxe, and then stand near a crafting table (carried inventory can place one using 2 wood) or use the existing torches in corners? Actually, the dungeon has torches in corners, but they are limited and may not be reachable. The agent must craft torches (1 wood + 1 coal) to extend its vision and arrows (1 wood + 1 stone) to replenish ammo. The only terminal goal remains descending to floor 2 (`ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES`). The pre‑supplied gear and completed overworld achievements remove any need for backtracking.

