      <data key="d10">1) Global Bottleneck Hypothesis (Objective Signal):
   The next critical progression gate is ENTER_SEWERS (floor 3). The global profile shows zero achievement for ENTER_SEWERS, indicating the agent cannot yet reach or survive floor 3. Unlocking sewers opens access to new enemies (lizards, kobolds), new loot, and eventually further floors (vaults, troll mines, realms), making it a high-value global bottleneck.

2) Parent Capability Frontier (What the parent proves):
   Under the scaffolded parent task (overworld→dungeon→enter gnomish mines), the agent can reliably navigate floors 0–1, defeat orcs, use torches/bow, and descend to floor 2 with stone tools and a low kill requirement (3 orcs). This demonstrates the agent has the basic combat, movement, and ladder-interaction skills needed for the next floor, provided similar scaffolding.

3) Diagnosis: Local vs Global (Avoid local traps):
   Local ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES SR is 54.75%, while global is only 16.12%. The local task design (pre‑unlocked ladder, stone tools, 3‑kill requirement) inflates success, so the low global rate does not necessarily indicate a missing prerequisite on earlier floors. Instead, it suggests the agent needs to learn the floor‑2 environment and combat to push further. The parent task also shows strong accidental skills (defeat_orc_solider 88.21%, open_chest 93.54%, etc.) that will transfer.

4) Evolution Choice: EXPAND.
   We add exactly one forward dependency beyond the parent frontier: entering the sewers from the gnomish mines. By starting on floor 2 with appropriate gear, we skip already‑mastered floors and focus on the new challenge (darkness, gnome enemies, and clearing the floor). The low kill count (3) keeps the task learnable while introducing the new enemies and descent condition. This is the logical thin‑slice expansion that directly improves global progression.

5) Scaffolding &amp; Backtracking Avoidance:
   The agent starts on floor 2 at the ladder‑up position. All prerequisites up to reaching floor 2 with an iron sword, stone pickaxe, bow, arrows, and torches are marked as Completed (including ENTER_DUNGEON, ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES, relevant crafting achievements). The initial inventory matches what a competent player would have upon arriving at floor 2. No backtracking to earlier floors is required; the task solely focuses on surviving, killing 3 gnomes, finding the down‑ladder, and descending.

6) Final Consistency Check:
   - Trained Task Relevant: ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES.
   - New Task Relevant: ENTER_SEWERS.
   - Completed: (list below).
   - “One‑main‑change”: Yes – only the new floor‑2‑to‑3 descent is added; everything else (tools, kill count) is a one‑off adjustment to make the frontier learnable.
   - Backtracking check: The agent never needs to go to earlier floors, so no backtracking.</data>
