      <data key="d2">Objective: Increase combat endurance on the Dungeon floor to the full‑game standard of 8 kills, under slightly relaxed survival pressure, preparing for reliable entry into the Gnomish Mines.

Description: The agent begins on Floor 1 (Dungeon) at the up‑ladder position holding an iron sword (inventory: `{"sword": 3}`). The dungeon layout is the default procedural generation, with the ladder‑down placed in its usual room. The descent to the Gnomish Mines remains locked until the agent defeats exactly eight hostile monsters (melee orc soldiers or ranged orc mages) on this level. Survival needs – hunger, thirst, fatigue – deplete at 70% of the normal Craftax rate (`needs_depletion_multiplier = 0.7`), giving the agent more focus on combat while still requiring occasional visits to snails and fountains. All other mechanics (mob spawn rates, health/damage multipliers, recovery rates) are left at their default 1.0. This task directly strengthens the agent’s ability to sustain prolonged combat on the first dungeon floor, targeting the full 8‑kill gate that must be passed in the original game.

Relevant Achievements: ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES
Completed Achievements: MAKE_IRON_SWORD, ENTER_DUNGEON

World:
- Player: Starting floor = 1 (via `builder.set_starting_floor(1)`). Inventory: `{"sword": 3}` (via `builder.set_player_inventory({"sword": 3})`). All other attributes default.
- Map:
  - No manual block placements; the default dungeon generation is left intact.
  - Kill counter is reset: `builder.set_monsters_killed(level=1, count=0)`.
- Mechanics:
  - `monsters_killed_to_clear_level = 8`
  - `needs_depletion_multiplier = 0.7`
  - All other TaskParams (passive/melee/ranged spawn multipliers, mob health/damage multipliers, health recover/loss/mana recover multipliers) remain at 1.0.</data>
      <data key="d3">import jax
from craftax.craftax.constants import Achievement
from craftax.craftax.craftax_state import EnvParams, StaticEnvParams

from minicraftax.craftax_state import EnvState, TaskParams
from minicraftax.tasks.base_task import BaseTask
from minicraftax.world_builder import WorldBuilder


class Env(BaseTask):
    """Objective: Increase combat endurance on the Dungeon floor to the full‑game standard of 8 kills, under slightly relaxed survival pressure, preparing for reliable entry into the Gnomish Mines.

Description: The agent begins on Floor 1 (Dungeon) at the up‑ladder position holding an iron sword (inventory: `{"sword": 3}`). The dungeon layout is the default procedural generation, with the ladder‑down placed in its usual room. The descent to the Gnomish Mines remains locked until the agent defeats exactly eight hostile monsters (melee orc soldiers or ranged orc mages) on this level. Survival needs – hunger, thirst, fatigue – deplete at 70% of the normal Craftax rate (`needs_depletion_multiplier = 0.7`), giving the agent more focus on combat while still requiring occasional visits to snails and fountains. All other mechanics (mob spawn rates, health/damage multipliers, recovery rates) are left at their default 1.0. This task directly strengthens the agent’s ability to sustain prolonged combat on the first dungeon floor, targeting the full 8‑kill gate that must be passed in the original game.

Relevant Achievements: ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES
Completed Achievements: MAKE_IRON_SWORD, ENTER_DUNGEON

World:
- Player: Starting floor = 1 (via `builder.set_starting_floor(1)`). Inventory: `{"sword": 3}` (via `builder.set_player_inventory({"sword": 3})`). All other attributes default.
- Map:
  - No manual block placements; the default dungeon generation is left intact.
  - Kill counter is reset: `builder.set_monsters_killed(level=1, count=0)`.
- Mechanics:
  - `monsters_killed_to_clear_level = 8`
  - `needs_depletion_multiplier = 0.7`
  - All other TaskParams (passive/melee/ranged spawn multipliers, mob health/damage multipliers, health recover/loss/mana recover multipliers) remain at 1.0.
"""

    def __init__(self, static_params: StaticEnvParams, params: EnvParams):
        super().__init__(static_params, params)
        self.relevant_achievements = [
            Achievement.ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES,
        ]
        self.completed_achievements = [
            Achievement.MAKE_IRON_SWORD,
            Achievement.ENTER_DUNGEON,
        ]
        self.label = "ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES"

    def get_task_params(self) -&gt; TaskParams:
        """Return custom parameters for this task."""
        return TaskParams(
            monsters_killed_to_clear_level=8,
            needs_depletion_multiplier=0.7,
        )

    def generate_world(self, rng: jax.Array) -&gt; EnvState:
        """Generates the world for the task."""
        rng, build_rng = jax.random.split(rng)

        builder = WorldBuilder(build_rng, self.static_params, self.params)

        # Start on floor 1 (Dungeon)
        builder.set_starting_floor(1)

        # Equip an iron sword (sword=3)
        builder.set_player_inventory({
            "sword": 3,
        })

        # Reset the kill counter on floor 1 to 0
        builder.set_monsters_killed(level=1, count=0)

        # No block modifications; default dungeon generation suffices

        state = builder.build(rng)

        # Mark pre-completed achievements as True
        achievements = state.achievements
        for ach in self.completed_achievements:
            achievements = achievements.at[ach.value].set(True)
        state = state.replace(achievements=achievements)

        return state</data>
