      <data key="d10">1) **Global Bottleneck Hypothesis (Objective Signal):**  
   The global profile shows ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES at only 16.67%, and DEFEAT_GNOME_WARRIOR at 0.15%. After descending into the Gnomish Mines, the agent is immediately killed by the first enemy encounter (Gnome Warrior or Gnome Archer). The next critical progression transition is surviving the initial combat on floor 2. Improving this should directly raise global floor-2 survival and subsequent resource gathering.

2) **Parent Capability Frontier (What the parent proves):**  
   The trained task shows the agent can reliably clear floor 1 (kill two Orc Soldiers and one Orc Mage) and manage survival (eat Snail, drink from fountains) while navigating the Dungeon, achieving descent about 53.59% of the time. Prerequisites like ENTER_DUNGEON, crafting a stone sword, and finding a bow are already covered, so we can safely start on floor 1 with that equipment to focus training forward.

3) **Diagnosis: Local vs Global (Avoid local traps):**  
   - **Local task performance:** Main goal SR 53.59%; defeat_orc_solider 95.88%, defeat_orc_mage 73.67%, ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES 53.59%.  
   - **Global performance:** defeat_orc_solider 84.70%, defeat_orc_mage 74.24%, ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES 16.67%, defeat_gnome_warrior 0.15%.  
   The drop from local descent to global descent suggests the agent still struggles when integrated into the full game, but the more urgent gap is the near‑zero ability to fight Gnome Warriors. Since dungeon fighting is already moderate, the priority is to train the immediate post‑descent combat.

4) **Evolution Choice (Expand):**  
   We expand by adding ONE forward dependency beyond the parent frontier: after entering the Gnomish Mines, the agent must defeat a single Gnome Warrior. This thin‑slice directly addresses the global bottleneck of floor‑2 survival. All other scaffolding (floor‑1 combat, equipment, survival rate) remains as in the parent, so the agent still practices the descent while gaining crucial early‑mines combat experience.

5) **Scaffolding &amp; Backtracking Avoidance:**  
   The agent starts on floor 1 with the same inventory (stone sword, bow, 10 arrows, 5 torches) and all needs at max, compressing the overworld‑to‑dungeon transition. No backtracking to floor 0 is required. The only new element is a single Gnome Warrior placed near the up‑ladder of floor 2, ensuring immediate but manageable exposure.

6) **Final Consistency Check:**  
   - Trained Task Relevant Achievements: DEFEAT_ORC_SOLIDER, DEFEAT_ORC_MAGE, ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES  
   - New Task Relevant Achievements: DEFEAT_ORC_SOLIDER, DEFEAT_ORC_MAGE, ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES, DEFEAT_GNOME_WARRIOR  
   - New Task Completed Achievements: ENTER_DUNGEON, MAKE_STONE_SWORD, FIND_BOW  
   - “One‑main‑change” check: YES – only one additional achievement (defeat gnome warrior) beyond parent.  
   - Backtracking check: YES – no need to go to earlier floors for prerequisites.</data>
