      <data key="d10">**Justification for New Evolutionary Task:** 
The agent has partial success locally (59.42%) on the full overworld‑to‑gnomish‑mines chain, but globally ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES is only 17.36%. The bottleneck is not conceptual understanding but fragility in the early tool‑tier steps (stone pickaxe 85% locally, iron‑sword crafting 55%). To raise transfer to the original game we need the agent to practice the later stages (dungeon clearance, descending) more reliably, which requires compressing the early, already partly‑reliable steps. Thus we scaffold by providing a stone pickaxe and a wood sword, reducing prerequisite failures while keeping the core challenge of iron‑sword crafting, furnace placement, dungeon combat, and descent intact. This is a **Persist** with one scaffolding change, increasing local success to give more repetitions on the global bottleneck transition.</data>
