      <data key="d2">Objective: Train the agent to robustly clear the Dungeon (Floor 1) under full‑difficulty conditions and descend to the Gnomish Mines (Floor 2).

Description: The agent spawns on Floor 1 (Dungeon) at the ladder‑up location. Its inventory contains a stone sword (tier 2) and a stone pickaxe (tier 2); all other inventory slots are empty. All attributes start at 1, status bars full, no enchantments, no learned spells. The agent must explore the procedurally‑generated Dungeon, defeat Orc Soldiers (melee) and Orc Mages (ranged) until 8 kills are reached to unlock the ladder down, then stand on the ladder and descend to Floor 2 (ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES). Unlike the previous easier version, **mob damage and needs depletion are set to their default (original Craftax) values**, forcing the agent to manage health, thirst, hunger, and fatigue at the full game’s pace and to engage enemies with standard damage output. No bow, arrows, torches, or other consumables are provided; the agent may scavenge them from chests or craft them using resources found on the floor. The primary skill being reinforced is **resilient melee‑and‑bow combat against multiple Orc types under sustained survival pressure**, which is the critical bottleneck for global progression beyond the Dungeon.

Relevant Achievements: ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES

Completed Achievements: COLLECT_WOOD, PLACE_TABLE, MAKE_WOOD_PICKAXE, COLLECT_STONE, MAKE_STONE_PICKAXE, MAKE_STONE_SWORD, ENTER_DUNGEON

