      <data key="d2">Objective: Learn to fight and defeat a Gnome Warrior inside the dark Gnomish Mines.

Description: The agent starts directly in the Gnomish Mines (floor 2) with a full inventory simulating a successful arrival: 1 iron sword, 1 bow, 10 arrows, 10 torches, 1 stone pickaxe, 10 cooked meat (or equivalent food to ignore hunger), and full health/mana/energy. A single torch is placed at the spawn coordinates to remove starting darkness. One gnome warrior is pre‑placed 4 tiles directly north of the spawn point on a valid ground tile. No other mobs of any kind will spawn (both passive, melee, and ranged spawn multipliers set to zero). Survival needs are negligible (`needs_depletion_multiplier = 0.1`, `health_loss_multiplier = 0.0`) so the agent can focus on combat. The only required achievement is to defeat the gnome warrior; the level‑clear requirement is set to 0 so there is no obligation to kill additional mobs. The agent must place torches to see the warrior, approach, and use its iron sword (or bow) to kill it. Mob health and damage are reduced to 0.8× to provide a forgiving introduction. Upon success, the task ends immediately.

Relevant Achievements: DEFEAT_GNOME_WARRIOR

Completed Achievements: ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES

World:
- Player:
  - `set_starting_floor(2)`
  - `set_player_inventory({"iron_sword": 1, "bow": 1, "arrows": 10, "torch": 10, "stone_pickaxe": 1, "cooked_meat": 10})`
  - `set_player_stats(strength=1, dexterity=1, intelligence=1)` (default)
  - Player health/food/drink/mana/energy all set to max.
- Map:
  - `place_block(2, BlockType.TORCH, (player_start_row, player_start_col))`  # ensures immediate light
  - `add_mobs_randomly_near(rng, 2, "melee", MobType.MELEE.value, 1, target_pos=(player_start_row + 4, player_start_col), min_dist=0, max_dist=1, on_blocks=[BlockType.PATH])`  # place gnome warrior exactly 4 tiles north, on a path block.
  - No other modifications; floor 2 default generation remains (pitch black, stalagmites, ores, etc.).
- Mechanics:
  - `monsters_killed_to_clear_level = 0`
  - `melee_spawn_multiplier = 0.0`
  - `ranged_spawn_multiplier = 0.0`
  - `passive_spawn_multiplier = 0.0`
  - `mob_health_multiplier = 0.8`
  - `mob_damage_multiplier = 0.8`
  - `needs_depletion_multiplier = 0.1`
  - `health_loss_multiplier = 0.0`
  - `melee_trigger_distance = 10`  # default, ensures warrior detects player
  - All other TaskParams at default.</data>
