      <data key="d2">Objective: Teach the agent to navigate the dark Gnomish Mines and defeat a Gnome Warrior using melee combat and torch placement.

Description: The agent starts on Floor 2 (Gnomish Mines) at the ladder‑up position. Inventory is set to a Stone Sword (tier 2), a Stone Pickaxe (tier 2), and 10 Torches. The map uses the standard SmoothGen mines generation: pitch‑black lighting, stalagmites (which yield stone), coal, iron, diamond, sapphire, and ruby ore deposits, and lava lakes. No additional ore blocks are placed. To guarantee immediate combat experience, three Gnome Warriors (melee, type_id = 1) are placed randomly on grass or path tiles within a Manhattan distance of 5 to 15 blocks from the player’s starting location (using `builder.add_mobs_randomly_near(...)`). Normal mob spawning remains active (melee and ranged multipliers = 1.0), so additional gnomes may appear naturally. The task terminates successfully when the agent earns the `DEFEAT_GNOME_WARRIOR` achievement. All prerequisite achievements for reaching this floor and obtaining stone‑tier equipment are marked as completed. Survival needs are relaxed (`needs_depletion_multiplier = 0.5`) to keep pressure low while the agent learns the new enemy. All other mechanics are left at default values.

Relevant Achievements: DEFEAT_GNOME_WARRIOR

Completed Achievements: ENTER_DUNGEON, ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES, PLACE_TABLE, COLLECT_WOOD, COLLECT_STONE, MAKE_WOOD_PICKAXE, MAKE_WOOD_SWORD, MAKE_STONE_PICKAXE, MAKE_STONE_SWORD

World:
- Player: `builder.set_starting_floor(2)`.  
  `builder.set_player_inventory({"sword": 2, "pickaxe": 2, "torch": 10})`.  
  All attributes default (full health, food, drink, etc.).
- Map:
  - No block modifications; the default SmoothGen Gnomish Mines layout is used.
  - `builder.add_mobs_randomly_near(rng, level=2, mob_name="gnome_warrior", type_id=1, n=3, min_dist=5, max_dist=15, on_blocks=[BlockType.GRASS, BlockType.PATH])`
- Mechanics:
  - `needs_depletion_multiplier = 0.5`
  - All other TaskParams are left at their defaults.</data>
