      <data key="d10">1) Global Bottleneck Hypothesis (Objective Signal):
The global performance shows a sharp drop from entering the Dungeon (91.45%) to entering the Gnomish Mines (16.03%). This bottleneck is likely due to the agent’s fragility under full hostile mob pressure while managing survival and executing the Stone‑Sword‑and‑clear cycle. Improving the agent’s ability to handle moderately increased hostile spawns during the Overworld‑to‑Gnomish‑Mines transition will directly raise global success rate on this crucial progression gate.

2) Parent Capability Frontier (What the parent proves):
The parent task shows the agent can, under half spawn rates, reliably gather wood/stone, craft a Stone Sword, defeat Dungeon mobs, and reach Floor 2 (60% SR). Wood Pickaxe crafting is already mastered globally (99.24%), so we can compress it away by starting with a Wood Pickaxe. The remaining prerequisites (survival basics, stone sword crafting) are known to be learnable under reduced pressure.

3) Diagnosis: Local vs Global (Avoid local traps):
Task‑specific SR on relevant achievements is high for crafting and Dungeon combat (defeat_orc_soldier 92.97%, defeat_orc_mage 89.73%), but global equivalents are significantly lower (85.65% and 73.44%). This discrepancy indicates that the 0.5 spawn multiplier masked a true combat fragility. The agent is not under‑skilled on survival basics (global collect_wood 100%) – the bottleneck is executing the full chain under increased combat pressure. We must raise spawn intensity to bridge the local‑to‑global gap.

4) Evolution Choice (Persist / Simplify / Expand / Vary):
We EXPAND by increasing hostile spawn multipliers from 0.5 to 0.75. This is a thin‑slice change: only one parameter (executional difficulty) is adjusted, while the goal, starting state, and other mechanics remain identical. This forces the agent to cope with more frequent and intense combat encounters without introducing any new dependencies or backtracking. The jump is small enough to remain learnable, directly targets the observed global weakness, and aligns with forward curriculum pressure.

5) Scaffolding &amp; Backtracking Avoidance (Start‑state design):
The initial state still provides a Wood Pickaxe, placing MAKE_WOOD_PICKAXE in Completed Achievements. No backtracking to floor 0 for basic crafting is required. The Overworld loop now demands the agent gather wood and stone under slightly heavier mob pressure, which will generalise to fulll‑game scenarios.

6) Final Consistency Check:
Trained Task Relevant Achievements: [ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES]
New Task Relevant Achievements: [ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES]
New Task Completed Achievements: [MAKE_WOOD_PICKAXE]
One‑main‑change: Only hostile spawn multipliers changed (0.5 → 0.75). YES
Backtracking: No requirement to revisit earlier floors for crafting prerequisites. YES</data>
