      <data key="d2">Objective: Practice chaining overworld preparation and Dungeon clearing under the **original Craftax survival dynamics**, enabling the agent to robustly enter the Gnomish Mines in the full game.

Description: The agent starts on Floor 0 (the Overworld) with a wood pickaxe, a wood sword, and a bow in inventory, simulating that basic early crafting has already been done. All life stats (food, drink, energy, health, mana) begin at 9/9, attributes are STR = 1, DEX = 1, INT = 1, and no spells are learned. No other items are provided. The agent must first gather stone, coal and wood on Floor 0 to craft a stone sword, at least one arrow, and at least one torch (using a crafting table). It must then locate the ladder down, enter the Dungeon (Floor 1), and fight through the orc soldiers and mages to kill the required number of monsters and find the ladder leading to Floor 2 (the Gnomish Mines). The crucial difference from the previous version of this task is that **all survival multipliers are now at their original Craftax values**: hunger, thirst and fatigue accumulate at the normal pace (needs_depletion_multiplier = 1.0), health regenerates at the base rate only when all needs are met (health_recover_multiplier = 1.0), and passive mobs (cows, snails) spawn at their regular frequency (passive_spawn_multiplier = 1.0). This removes the lenient survival scaffolding and forces the agent to manage food, drink, and energy while conducting the entire overworld‑to‑mines sequence.

