      <data key="d2">Objective: Survive the dark Gnomish Mines, defeat its gnome guardians, and descend to the Sewers for the first time.

Description: The agent begins on floor 2 (Gnomish Mines) at the position of the up‑ladder from floor 1. It carries the equipment of a capable adventurer: a stone sword, a stone pickaxe, a bow, 10 arrows, 5 torches, 3 cooked meat (represented as full food value; no actual “cooked meat” item exists, so we set `food` status to 9 and provide ample starting hunger/thirst/energy to simulate having eaten), and full water. All basic needs start at maximum (health 9, food 9, drink 9, energy 9, mana 9). Attributes are strength 1, dexterity 1, intelligence 1. The world is generated with the default 9‑level layout, but all block placements use standard generation for floor 2 (path/stone mix, stalagmites, darkness, ores). On floor 2, the agent must mine coal if necessary to craft more torches, but the initial 5 torches are enough to light its way. To unlock the ladder down to the Sewers (floor 3), the agent must defeat only 2 hostile gnomes (Gnome Warrior or Gnome Archer) – a much lower requirement than the full game, allowing focused combat practice. After meeting the kill count, the agent must locate the Ladder Down on floor 2, stand on it, and use DESCEND. Reaching floor 3 for the first time (ENTER_SEWERS) ends the episode successfully. Failure occurs if the agent dies or time expires.

Relevant Achievements: ENTER_SEWERS

Completed Achievements: COLLECT_WOOD, PLACE_TABLE, MAKE_WOOD_PICKAXE, MAKE_WOOD_SWORD, COLLECT_STONE, PLACE_STONE, MAKE_STONE_PICKAXE, MAKE_STONE_SWORD, PLACE_FURNACE, COLLECT_COAL, MAKE_TORCH, PLACE_TORCH, ENTER_DUNGEON, ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES, FIND_BOW, MAKE_ARROW, FIRE_BOW (initial bow/arrows assumed)

World:
- Player: start_floor = 2. Inventory: "stone_sword": 1, "stone_pickaxe": 1, "bow": 1, "arrows": 10, "torch": 5. Stats: strength=1, dexterity=1, intelligence=1. All needs at maximum (9/9).
- Map: No block modifications; use default level generation for all floors.
- Mechanics:
  - monsters_killed_to_clear_level = 2 (applies to all floors, but only floor 2 matters here)
  - All other TaskParams at default values (mob_health_multiplier = 1.0, mob_damage_multiplier = 1.0, melee_spawn_multiplier = 1.0, ranged_spawn_multiplier = 1.0, passive_spawn_multiplier = 1.0, needs_depletion_multiplier = 1.0, etc.).</data>
      <data key="d3">import jax
from craftax.craftax.constants import Achievement
from craftax.craftax.craftax_state import EnvParams, StaticEnvParams

from minicraftax.craftax_state import EnvState, TaskParams
from minicraftax.tasks.base_task import BaseTask
from minicraftax.world_builder import WorldBuilder


class Env(BaseTask):
    """Objective: Survive the dark Gnomish Mines, defeat its gnome guardians, and descend to the Sewers for the first time.

Description: The agent begins on floor 2 (Gnomish Mines) at the position of the up‑ladder from floor 1. It carries the equipment of a capable adventurer: a stone sword, a stone pickaxe, a bow, 10 arrows, 5 torches, 3 cooked meat (represented as full food value; no actual “cooked meat” item exists, so we set `food` status to 9 and provide ample starting hunger/thirst/energy to simulate having eaten), and full water. All basic needs start at maximum (health 9, food 9, drink 9, energy 9, mana 9). Attributes are strength 1, dexterity 1, intelligence 1. The world is generated with the default 9‑level layout, but all block placements use standard generation for floor 2 (path/stone mix, stalagmites, darkness, ores). On floor 2, the agent must mine coal if necessary to craft more torches, but the initial 5 torches are enough to light its way. To unlock the ladder down to the Sewers (floor 3), the agent must defeat only 2 hostile gnomes (Gnome Warrior or Gnome Archer) – a much lower requirement than the full game, allowing focused combat practice. After meeting the kill count, the agent must locate the Ladder Down on floor 2, stand on it, and use DESCEND. Reaching floor 3 for the first time (ENTER_SEWERS) ends the episode successfully. Failure occurs if the agent dies or time expires.

Relevant Achievements: ENTER_SEWERS

Completed Achievements: COLLECT_WOOD, PLACE_TABLE, MAKE_WOOD_PICKAXE, MAKE_WOOD_SWORD, COLLECT_STONE, PLACE_STONE, MAKE_STONE_PICKAXE, MAKE_STONE_SWORD, PLACE_FURNACE, COLLECT_COAL, MAKE_TORCH, PLACE_TORCH, ENTER_DUNGEON, ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES, FIND_BOW, MAKE_ARROW, FIRE_BOW (initial bow/arrows assumed)

World:
- Player: start_floor = 2. Inventory: "stone_sword": 1, "stone_pickaxe": 1, "bow": 1, "arrows": 10, "torch": 5. Stats: strength=1, dexterity=1, intelligence=1. All needs at maximum (9/9).
- Map: No block modifications; use default level generation for all floors.
- Mechanics:
  - monsters_killed_to_clear_level = 2 (applies to all floors, but only floor 2 matters here)
  - All other TaskParams at default values (mob_health_multiplier = 1.0, mob_damage_multiplier = 1.0, melee_spawn_multiplier = 1.0, ranged_spawn_multiplier = 1.0, passive_spawn_multiplier = 1.0, needs_depletion_multiplier = 1.0, etc.).
"""

    def __init__(self, static_params: StaticEnvParams, params: EnvParams):
        super().__init__(static_params, params)
        self.relevant_achievements = [
            Achievement.ENTER_SEWERS,
        ]
        self.completed_achievements = [
            Achievement.COLLECT_WOOD,
            Achievement.PLACE_TABLE,
            Achievement.MAKE_WOOD_PICKAXE,
            Achievement.MAKE_WOOD_SWORD,
            Achievement.COLLECT_STONE,
            Achievement.PLACE_STONE,
            Achievement.MAKE_STONE_PICKAXE,
            Achievement.MAKE_STONE_SWORD,
            Achievement.PLACE_FURNACE,
            Achievement.COLLECT_COAL,
            Achievement.MAKE_TORCH,
            Achievement.PLACE_TORCH,
            Achievement.ENTER_DUNGEON,
            Achievement.ENTER_GNOMISH_MINES,
            Achievement.FIND_BOW,
            Achievement.MAKE_ARROW,
            Achievement.FIRE_BOW,
        ]
        self.label = "ENTER_SEWERS"

    def get_task_params(self) -&gt; TaskParams:
        """Return custom parameters for this task."""
        return TaskParams(
            monsters_killed_to_clear_level=2,
        )

    def generate_world(self, rng: jax.Array) -&gt; EnvState:
        """Generates the world for the task."""
        rng, build_rng = jax.random.split(rng)

        builder = WorldBuilder(build_rng, self.static_params, self.params)

        # Start on floor 2 (Gnomish Mines)
        builder.set_starting_floor(2)

        # Equip starting inventory: stone sword, stone pickaxe, bow, arrows, torches
        builder.set_player_inventory({
            "sword": 2,      # stone sword
            "pickaxe": 2,    # stone pickaxe
            "bow": 1,
            "arrows": 10,
            "torches": 5,
        })

        # No block/mob modifications – default world generation
        state = builder.build(rng)

        # Mark pre‑completed achievements as True
        achievements = state.achievements
        for ach in self.completed_achievements:
            achievements = achievements.at[ach.value].set(True)
        state = state.replace(achievements=achievements)

        return state</data>
